{"_id":"08Ub5ON3KRAgnBbD","name":"Barren Dorn","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:barren-dorn","level":6,"monsterType":"Magitech","intelligence":"Servant","perception":"Mechanical","disposition":"Instructed","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Ruins","reputation":13,"weakness":16,"weakPoint":"Lightning damage +3 points","initiative":12,"movementSpeed":"16 (Wheeled)","fortitude":"8 (15)","willpower":"8 (15)","source":"CR II p. 384","description":"This is an even larger version of the Dorn series, with a mobile mechanism attached to its base. It was prepared for combat, and there are records of its use in large-scale battles against Barbarous. Few still exist, and their remnants are sometimes found in ruins or Barbarous territory.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Blade (Right Side)","accuracy":"8 (15)","damage":"2d+6","evasion":"7 (14)","defense":6,"hp":{"value":49,"max":49},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}},{"style":"Hammer (Left Side)","accuracy":"8 (15)","damage":"2d+9","evasion":"7 (14)","defense":6,"hp":{"value":49,"max":49},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}},{"style":"Wheels (Wheels)","accuracy":"9 (16)","damage":"2d+7","evasion":"6 (13)","defense":8,"hp":{"value":43,"max":43},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"All Sections","description":""},{"title":"◯ Mechanical Body","description":"It is immune to criticals from edged weapons."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Magitech HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Magitech's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Magitech can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."},{"title":"Right Side","description":""},{"title":"🗨 Red-hot Blade","description":"Blade becomes red-hot. If the attack hits, the damage dealt will be fire type, and the target's Defense will be treated as halved (rounded up)."},{"title":"Left Side","description":""},{"title":"► Hammer Throw &amp; Pull Back/7 (14)/Evasion/Negates","description":"It can throw a hammer and immediately pull it back.\nWith &quot;Target: 1 Character&quot; and &quot;Range/Area: 1 (10m)/ Shot &quot; deals 2d+7 physical damage.\nThe section that uses this ability takes a -1 penalty to its Evasion check until the beginning of its next turn."},{"title":"Wheels","description":""},{"title":"◯ Slalom Drive","description":"Wheel attacks can be made on up to two targets at the same time; Accuracy checks are made only once at a time, and damage should be determined individually."},{"title":"► Random Drive","description":"Until the beginning of the next turn, the Right Side and Left Side gain a +2 bonus to Evasion checks.\nThis ability cannot be used on consecutive turns."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Iron (20G/Black B) x 3"},{"roll":"2 - 7","loot":"Crude Magitech Components (100G/Black White A)"},{"roll":"8 - 11","loot":"Magitech Components (300G/Black White A)"},{"roll":"12+","loot":"Rare Magitech Components (900G/Black White A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Barren Dorn","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"3VlNzhE9fo3eegRV","name":"Maginohek","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:maginohek","level":11,"monsterType":"Magitech","intelligence":"Servant","perception":"Mechanical","disposition":"Instructed","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Ruins, Plains","reputation":18,"weakness":21,"weakPoint":"Magic damage +2 points","initiative":17,"movementSpeed":"10 (4 legs)","fortitude":"15 (22)","willpower":"14 (21)","source":"Monstrous Lore p. 169","description":"Maginohek is essentially a self-propelled &quot;wall.&quot;\n\nIt features four legs on the back side of a square wall measuring about 5 meters on each side. When in motion, it walks flat on its back, and it is possible to place materials or soldier gunners on top of it.\n\nOriginally, several Maginohek were operated simultaneously, with their role being to construct makeshift field fortifications. To achieve this, several Maginohek would stand on two legs and interweave their remaining two legs with each other in a horizontal line.\n\nThe Maginohek is equipped with several inlays, through which another magitech soldier or shooter can attack using guns. However, the Maginohek seen today lacks accompanying soldiers and attacks with spears and other weapons. It has a balance issue, and when it stands on two legs, it is highly prone to falling over on its own.\n\nAlthough they can be seen at the remains of military bases, they are currently few in number and rarely form huge walls. Even so, their defenses are extremely hard, and getting caught in a fall by accident could easily result in being crushed to death.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Spear","accuracy":"15 (22)","damage":"2d+18","evasion":"10 (17)","defense":20,"hp":{"value":200,"max":200},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Water/Ice Immunity , ◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Mechanical Body","description":"It is immune to criticals from edged weapons."},{"title":"◯ Limited 3 Attacks","description":"Maginohek can make three Spear attacks with one Major Action.\nIt can only choose the same target twice in the same round."},{"title":"◯ Giant Wall","description":"Maginohek counts as 5 characters for the purpose of determining blocking movement and the size of the skirmish area."},{"title":"⏩ △ Morphogenesis","description":"This monster has two forms, the &quot;Mobile Form&quot; and the &quot;Combat Form&quot;, which can be changed to each other with Minor Action or during Combat Preparation. In each turn, the Maginohek can perform [ ⏩ △ Morphogenesis] only once.\nMaginohek cannot make Melee Attack cannot be performed in Mobile Form. Also, it gains [ ◯ Mounted = 3 Characters].\nMelee Attack can be performed in Combat Form. Also, Maginohek gets the [ ◯ Gun-Proof Armor]."},{"title":"◯ Mounted = 3 Characters","description":"Up to 3 characters can be mounted .\nThis ability is only available when the Maginohek is in Mobile Form. If a character is mounted and then [ ⏩ △ Morphogenesis] is used to change into Combat Form, all mounted characters will fall off this monster (see CR III, p. 89)."},{"title":"◯ Gun-Proof Armor","description":"Defense is useful when the Maginohek receives magic damage from Ranged Attacks, Area: Shot , or Area: Line spells or effects.\nThis ability can be obtained only when Maginohek is in Combat Form."},{"title":"◯ Out of Balance/14 (21)/Evasion/Negates","description":"Maginohek can fall prone depending on its HP.\nRoll 1d at the start of the turn, and Maginohek will fall prone depending on its HP and the roll. If it falls prone, it deals 2d+30 physical damage to &quot;Target: 1 area(Radius 6m) / 20&quot; within &quot;Range: Caster&quot;. After that, it changes to the Moving Form.\nThe Maginohek needs a Major Action to get up from the fall, and cannot perform [ ⏩ △ Morphogenesis] on turn it fell from this ability.\nTumbling Table\nCurrent HP | 1d Roll |\n151 or more | 1 |\n101 – 150 | 1 – 2 |\n51 – 100 | 1 – 3 |\n50 or less | 1 – 4 |"},{"title":"◯ Collapse of a Giant Wall","description":"The number of experience points earned by defeating this monster is 220 per character."},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Magitech HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Magitech's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Magitech can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Mysterious Magitech Components (2,400G/Black White S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Maginohek","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"7b9i3jOftKNE4EgZ","name":"Gichas","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:gichas","level":4,"monsterType":"Magitech","intelligence":"Servant","perception":"Mechanical","disposition":"Instructed","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Ruins, Shallows","reputation":12,"weakness":14,"weakPoint":"Lightning damage +3 points","initiative":11,"movementSpeed":"15 (Wheels)","fortitude":"6 (13)","willpower":"5 (12)","source":"AB, p. 109","description":"This Magitech has a tetrahedral body and three spherical feet similar to a Cuir , but differs in having two arms equipped with large blades. These two blades can cross to function as large scissors.\n\nIt is a mass-produced Magitech soldier developed simultaneously with Cuir for subjugating the Shallow Abyss. Originally, it was designed to conduct reconnaissance using Cuir and attack any discovered threats. However, like Cuir, it lost its remote control capabilities and went berserk within Shallow Abysses. Now it considers anyone coming from outside the Shallows as enemies and attacks indiscriminately. While most roam alone, sometimes multiple units gather and attack in groups.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Blade","accuracy":"6(13)","damage":"2d+5","evasion":"&#32;","defense":5,"hp":{"value":5,"max":5},"mp":{"value":32,"max":32}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Mechanical Body","description":"It is immune to criticals from edged weapons."},{"title":"◯All-Terrain Movement","description":"Ignore terrain penalties up to -2 (penalties worse than -3 still apply)."},{"title":"◯Double Action","description":"Can perform 2 Major Actions in 1 round."},{"title":"►Scissor Cut / 7 (14) / Evasion / Negates","description":"This attack can only be performed against a character who has been hit by Blade during Gichas' turn.\nWhile pinning the target with the blade that hit, it attacks in a scissoring motion with its other blade to deal 2d+10 points of physical damage."},{"title":"◯Poison Immunity, ◯Disease Immunity, ◯Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Magitech HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Magitech's HP."},{"title":"◯Can Be Detected","description":"Magitech can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Iron (20G/Black B)"},{"roll":"2 - 5","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"6 - 9","loot":"Crude Magitech Components (100G/Black White A)"},{"roll":"10+","loot":"Magitech Components (300G/Black White A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Gichas","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"Bx4Gyne6GftgoryH","name":"Gur Barba","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:gur-barba","level":6,"monsterType":"Magitech","intelligence":"Servant","perception":"Mechanical","disposition":"Instructed","soulscars":0,"languages":"Magitech","habitat":"Ruins, Mountains","reputation":13,"weakness":16,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":13,"movementSpeed":"-/10(Floating)","fortitude":"7 (14)","willpower":"7 (14)","source":"CR III p. 385","description":"This large Barba is about one meter in length and holds a Bursting Shell and a restore fluid to support front-line Magitech. The fluid solidifies quickly when it touches the damaged part of the Magitech and closes it temporarily.\n\nBoth Bursting Shell and the restore liquid are loaded only enough for one use.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Legs","accuracy":"9 (16)","damage":"2d+8","evasion":"8 (15)","defense":5,"hp":{"value":48,"max":48},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"► Bursting Shell Drop/8 (15)/Willpower/ Half","description":"The bursting shell is dropped on the top of the target. Within &quot;Range: Caster&quot; deals 2d+7 Fire magic damage to &quot;Target: 1 area (3m Radius) / 5&quot;.\nThis ability can only be used once."},{"title":"► Sprinkle Repair Liquid/Can't","description":"Sprays Magitech restoring liquid to &quot;Target: 1 area (3m Radius) / 5&quot; in &quot;Range: Caster.&quot; If the target is a Magitech character, its HP is restored by 2d+7 points.\nThis effect can be used only once. This monster is always excluded from this effect."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Magitech HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Magitech's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Magitech can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Iron (20G/Black B)"},{"roll":"2 - 7","loot":"Crude Magitech Components (100G/Black White A)"},{"roll":"8+","loot":"Magitech Components (300G/Black White A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Gur Barba","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"CgbRMEoRMUz56MHD","name":"Deg Kagner","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:deg-kagner","level":5,"monsterType":"Magitech","intelligence":"Servant","perception":"Mechanical","disposition":"Instructed","soulscars":0,"languages":"Magitech","habitat":"Ruins","reputation":12,"weakness":15,"weakPoint":"Lightning damage + 3 points","initiative":11,"movementSpeed":"10 (Wheeled)","fortitude":"7 (14)","willpower":"7 (14)","source":"CR III p. 385","description":"This sturdy Kagner is designed for transportation over rough terrain, such as mountains and wastelands. The extra fence to secure the Magitech to be transported is added to protect the Magitech even more firmly.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Slam","accuracy":"7 (14)","damage":"2d+7","evasion":"7 (14)","defense":7,"hp":{"value":42,"max":42},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Mechanical Body","description":"It is immune to criticals from edged weapons."},{"title":"◯ Mounted Magitech = 2 Characters","description":"Up to 2 Magitech characters (2 sections) can be mounted ."},{"title":"◯ Mounted Person Protection = +2 • +2","description":"A character mounted on this monster has a +2 bonus to Evasion checks against melee and ranged attacks."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Magitech HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Magitech's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Magitech can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Iron (20G/Black B)"},{"roll":"2 - 8","loot":"Crude Magitech Components (100G/Black White A)"},{"roll":"9+","loot":"Magitech Components (300G/Black White A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Deg Kagner","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"DKfz19FyLceiUfCJ","name":"Gershuls","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:gershuls","level":11,"monsterType":"Magitech","intelligence":"Servant","perception":"Mechanical","disposition":"Instructed","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Shallows","reputation":18,"weakness":21,"weakPoint":"Slashing type damage +3 points","initiative":18,"movementSpeed":"-/20 (Floating)","fortitude":"15 (22)","willpower":"14 (21)","source":"AB, p. 114","description":"Gershuls is an ambitious magical machine designed to enter the Shallow Abyss and neutralize the power of the Abyss by sealing the Abyss Core itself within its hull, while utilizing it as a power source. Dozens of units were constructed and actually deployed in Shallow Abyss suppression operations.\n\nWith a total length exceeding 20m, it has a smooth, streamlined ship form that moves by floating. Its center contains a special storage bay that can house the Abyss Core.\n\nThe front end is sharply pointed, enabling powerful ramming attacks. The hull also features multiple bomb bays for bombing runs. Additionally, it is equipped with two multi-purpose work arms that can be used for everything from securing the Abyss Core to self-defense and hull repairs.\n\nWhile Gershuls deployed in Shallows succeeded in storing the Abyss Core within their hulls, most of them went berserk as a result, and began wandering aimlessly within the Shallow.\n\nIn some cases, they succeeded in making the Shallow disappear by storing the Abyss Core, but there were instances where they would then appear on the surface and trigger tragic incidents by creating new Shallows in different locations.\n\nThe Gershuls act to protect the Abyss Core, even summoning Daemons as guards. It views anyone targeting the Abyss Core as an enemy and attack them ferociously.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Ram (Ram)","accuracy":"13(20)","damage":"2d+15","evasion":"&#32;","defense":13,"hp":{"value":16,"max":16},"mp":{"value":32,"max":32}},{"style":"None (Hull)","accuracy":"-","damage":"-","evasion":"&#32;","defense":12,"hp":{"value":10,"max":10},"mp":{"value":32,"max":32}},{"style":"Arm (Arm)","accuracy":"14(21)","damage":"2d+12","evasion":"&#32;","defense":13,"hp":{"value":12,"max":12},"mp":{"value":32,"max":32}},{"style":"Arm (Arm)","accuracy":"14(21)","damage":"2d+12","evasion":"&#32;","defense":13,"hp":{"value":12,"max":12},"mp":{"value":32,"max":32}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"All Sections","description":""},{"title":"◯Poison Immunity, ◯Disease Immunity, ◯Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Magitech HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Magitech's HP."},{"title":"◯Can Be Detected","description":"Magitech can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."},{"title":"Ram &amp; Arm","description":""},{"title":"◯Mechanical Body","description":"All Arms and Ram sections are immune to critical hits from edged weapons."},{"title":"◯Aerial Standby","description":"If both Ram and Arms sections end their turn without performing a melee attack, no section of this monster can be targeted by melee attacks for the next 10 seconds (1 round)."},{"title":"Ram","description":""},{"title":"►Ram Attack / 15 (22) / Evasion / Negates","description":"This effect can only be used if the monster was in [◯Aerial Standby] state in the previous turn.\nPerform a melee attack against &quot;Target: 1 Character&quot; and deal 2d+20 points of physical damage."},{"title":"Hull","description":""},{"title":"►Bombardment / 13 (20) / Willpower / Half","description":"Within &quot;Range/Area: 1(20m) / Target &quot;, drops bombs on &quot;Target: 1 area (3m radius) / 5&quot;, dealing 2d+10 points of Fire and Bludgeoning magic damage.\nAll sections of this monster are automatically excluded from this effect's target."},{"title":"►Guardian Daemon (Shallow)","description":"This effect can only be used within the Shallow Abyss. Summons 1 Daemon. The summoned Daemon is determined by the following table, and the MP cost required for summoning varies by Daemon. If the required MP cannot be consumed, the Major Action ends wastefully. Additionally, if a Daemon summoned by this effect already exists on the battlefield, this effect cannot be used again.\n1d | Daemon | MP |\n1 | Godbell | 18 |\n2 | Shabalay | 18 |\n3 | Ragnakang | 36 |\n4 | Selassaroui | 20 |\n5 | Mahatiga | 35 |\n6 | Melbiz | 29 |\nThe summoned Daemon will not leave its position and will act according to its own judgment to protect Gershuls and eliminate their enemies. However, it will not take any actions to restore HP or MP for any section of this monster.\nThis effect lasts for only 3 minutes (18 rounds). After that, the Daemon is released and begins to act entirely according to its own judgment. At this time, the first thing the Daemon will do is swiftly leave this monster's side. Once this state is reached, even if that Daemon still exists, this monster can summon a new Daemon."},{"title":"Arm","description":""},{"title":"►Air Bullet / 12 (19) / Willpower / Half","description":"This effect consumes 1 MP per use.\nWith &quot;Range/Area: 1 (10m) / Shot &quot;, fires compressed air and deals 2d+8 points of Wind magic damage to &quot;Target: 1 Character.&quot;"},{"title":"►Hull Repair","description":"This effect consumes 8 MP points to use.\nRestores 2d+15 HP points to Hull section."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Iron Ingot (100G/Black B)"},{"roll":"Always","loot":"Abyss Shard (200G/-)"},{"roll":"2 - 9","loot":"Mysterious Magitech Components (2,400G/Black White S)"},{"roll":"10+","loot":"Trove of Magical Components (7,600G/Black White S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Gershuls","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"DgV3H7i2WzTzcPmV","name":"Vox Worker","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:vox-worker","level":3,"monsterType":"Magitech","intelligence":"High","perception":"Mechanical","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"Magitech","habitat":"Ruins","reputation":11,"weakness":14,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":9,"movementSpeed":"15 (Many Legs)","fortitude":"5 (12)","willpower":"4 (11)","source":"Natural History of Burlight p. 128","description":"Voxes are intelligent Magitech creatures that originated from the runaway self-healing subfunctions of the Magic Giant Colossus, the source of the Ward of Magic Giant in the Burlight Region. They resemble beetles with multiple long legs, but their upper body appears human-like, with a shell and features such as a face, torso, and arms.\n\nAll Voxes are descendants of the Vox Empress, who first separated from the Magic Giant Colossus. They continue to multiply by splitting from the Empress and the higher-ranking Vox Queens.\n\nVoxes function as a collective, sharing thoughts and perceptions among themselves. Therefore, when engaging in combat with the Vox, you will face a large number of them unless you defeat and escape before the surrounding Voxes gather or unless you sever their signal link.\n\nWhile the Vox Empress remains stationary at the far end of the Ward of Magic Giant, it is the Vox Queen who leads the Vox Soldiers, Vox Guards, and Vox Workers. Their influence appears to be expanding not only within the Ward but also in the surrounding areas.\n\nAlthough the Vox look down on races that do not share the same thoughts and perceptions as &quot;lower races,&quot; their beliefs are not non-negotiable. However, if you do negotiate, you will face very unfavorable conditions. If you pledge to work for Voxes, similar to a slave, you may receive protection.\n\nIn rare cases, there are also individuals who have lost their thinking and signal links and have deviated from the group. Some of these individuals are said to be more similar to Humanoids.\n\nThe Signal Circuit loot obtained from Vox is used as material for the Self-injuring Instruction Circuit (see Natural History of Burlight p. 42).","combatStyles":[{"style":"Slam","accuracy":"5 (12)","damage":"2d+2","evasion":"4 (11)","defense":5,"hp":{"value":23,"max":23},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Iron Body","description":"The Vox Worker is immune to criticals from edged weapons."},{"title":"◯Repair and Regeneration","description":"If the monster's HP is 10 or less at the beginning of their turn, the GM rolls 1d.\nIf the roll is &quot;1,&quot; the effect of [◯Repair Malfunction] occurs.\nIf the roll is &quot;2-6,&quot; HP is restored by 5."},{"title":"◯Repair Malfunction","description":"This effect occurs automatically on a roll of 1 during [◯Repair and Regeneration].\nThe monster's Accuracy increases by +2, and its damage is increased by +2 as well.\nImmediately after this effect occurs, the monster loses both [◯Repair and Regeneration] and [◯Emergency Signal]."},{"title":"◯Emergency Signal","description":"This effect occurs automatically when the monster's HP falls to 0 or less. The GM rolls 1d immediately. Assuming the roll is X: after X rounds, X/2 (rounded up) Vox Workers will appear on the battlefield (e.g., if the roll is 3, 2 will appear after 3 rounds).\nRounds are counted starting with the next monster faction round. In other words, if the roll was 1, a new monster will appear on the battlefield when the monster faction's next turn starts.\nIn Simplified Combat, the new monster(s) will appear in the Rearguard area of the monster's faction. In Standard or Advanced Combat, the position is 15m from the monster that used this ability, in any direction the GM decides (generally, the farther away from the PCs the better, but if the GM thinks it is geographically possible, they may also stage a surprise attack from behind).\nThis effect will not occur in the following cases:\nIf the damage that made the monster's HP 0 or less was Lightning type.\nWhen a monster whose HP is 0 or less is in the state of [◯Repair Malfunction].\nWhen any kind of Vox is already due to appear because of [◯Emergency Signal]. In this case, even if multiple Voxes have their HPs at 0 or below at the same time, the dice are rolled only for 1 character chosen by the GM. Note that this effect can occur again after a new Vox has already appeared.\nA new Vox from this effect will not appear if the battle ends before it arrives (hence, the last monster defeated will not cause this effect)."},{"title":"◯Delicate Loot","description":"If Lightning-type damage is dealt to this monster at least once, the loot &quot;Signal Circuit&quot; will be changed to &quot;Broken Magitech Components (50G/Black B).&quot;"},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Magitech HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Magitech's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Magitech can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Signal Circuit (100G/Black White A)"},{"roll":"2 - 8","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"9+","loot":"Crude Magitech Components (100G/Black White A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Vox Worker","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"ErGZInbCAw8i1QVe","name":"Dimateravia","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:dimateravia","level":9,"monsterType":"Magitech","intelligence":"Servant","perception":"Mechanical","disposition":"Instructed","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Ruins","reputation":18,"weakness":21,"weakPoint":"Magic damage +2 points","initiative":16,"movementSpeed":"5 (4 Legs)","fortitude":"11 (18)","willpower":"11 (18)","source":"CR II p. 387","description":"This Magitech is designed as an installed trap that dampens the mana of an object that has been stepped into. It has a spherical body with four short legs.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Fist","accuracy":"11 (18)","damage":"2d+10","evasion":"11 (18)","defense":13,"hp":{"value":84,"max":84},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Mana Diffusion","description":"Whenever a character within &quot;All Areas (Radius 30m)&quot; of this monster's center performs an action that consumes MP, the amount of MP consumed is increased by +1 point. When doubled by [ Metamagic/ ] or a similar effect, the original MP consumption is increased by +1 point and then doubled."},{"title":"► Maximum Disturbance/11 (18)/Willpower/Negates","description":"With &quot;Range: Caster&quot; and &quot;Target: all areas (30m radius) / All,&quot; creates an area that inhibits the use of mana. Whenever the target performs an action that consumes MP, it takes the same amount of fixed damage to its HP.\nThis effect is a curse type and lasts only for 10 seconds (1 round). Also, this unique skill cannot be used on consecutive turns."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Magitech HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Magitech's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Magitech can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Iron (20G/Black B)"},{"roll":"2 - 7","loot":"Rare Magitech Components (900G/Black White A)"},{"roll":"8+","loot":"Mysterious Magitech Components (2,400G/Black White S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Dimateravia","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"F4M7d0iqqak7neHd","name":"Renguard","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:renguard","level":1,"monsterType":"Magitech","intelligence":"Servant","perception":"Mechanical","disposition":"Instructed","soulscars":0,"languages":"Magitech","habitat":"Ruins","reputation":7,"weakness":12,"weakPoint":"Lightning Damage +3","initiative":7,"movementSpeed":"16 (Wheeled) / -","fortitude":"2 (9)","willpower":"2 (9)","source":"BM","description":"These small robots were simple security devices designed for use during the Magitech Civilization period. Sporting four short legs with wheels coming off a flat body, these robots will first attempt to drive away intruders using a simple warning in the Magitech language but will resort to electric shocks (Defense still applies) if this warning is not heeded.\n\nRenguards, while small, often appear in large numbers and will often link to each other in order to increase the power of their electric shocks and drive away more formidable intruders.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Electric Shock","accuracy":"3 (10)","damage":"2d-2","evasion":"2 (9)","defense":1,"hp":{"value":15,"max":15},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"► Linking","description":"The Renguard connects to a fellow Renguard within &quot;Range: Touch&quot; and increases its attack power. The targeted Renguard receives a +1 bonus to Accuracy checks and +3 bonus to damage. Up to 5 Renguards can be Linked together (4 Renguards to another) this way, for a 7 (14) Accuracy, dealing 2d+10 damage.\nAfter the boosted Renguard attacks, all Links are disconnected."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Magitech HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Magitech's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Magitech can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 9","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"10+","loot":"Old Recording Device (100G / Black White A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Renguard","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"G5brOT1pIwSCogqM","name":"Dragon Fortress","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:dragon-fortress","level":15,"monsterType":"Magitech","intelligence":"Servant","perception":"Mechanical","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"Magitech","habitat":"Ruins","reputation":17,"weakness":20,"weakPoint":"Lightning damage + 3 points","initiative":22,"movementSpeed":"20/50 (Flying)","fortitude":"21 (28)","willpower":"19 (26)","source":"CR III p. 390","description":"A large construct in the shape of a dragon, the Dragon Fortress is a huge machine, measuring around 50m long and 15m high. Able to fly at high speeds, its weapons are able to cause destruction on a massive scale. It is thought to be the top of the line when it comes to mobile defense and comes outfitted with a wide variety of weapons. It is an existence that brings together the highest level of technology in Magitech Civilization, and the leaders of each country are searching for their whereabouts.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Bite (Head)","accuracy":"17 (24)","damage":"2d+16","evasion":"18 (25)","defense":13,"hp":{"value":145,"max":145},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}},{"style":"Main Battery (Body)","accuracy":"19 (26)","damage":"2d+18","evasion":"16 (23)","defense":11,"hp":{"value":141,"max":141},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}},{"style":"Main Battery (Body)","accuracy":"19 (26)","damage":"2d+18","evasion":"16 (23)","defense":11,"hp":{"value":141,"max":141},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}},{"style":"Machine Gun (Wing)","accuracy":"20 (27)","damage":"2d+16","evasion":"17 (24)","defense":12,"hp":{"value":104,"max":104},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}},{"style":"Machine Gun (Wing)","accuracy":"20 (27)","damage":"2d+16","evasion":"17 (24)","defense":12,"hp":{"value":104,"max":104},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}},{"style":"Claw (Foot)","accuracy":"18 (25)","damage":"2d+17","evasion":"17 (24)","defense":10,"hp":{"value":119,"max":119},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}},{"style":"Claw (Foot)","accuracy":"18 (25)","damage":"2d+17","evasion":"17 (24)","defense":10,"hp":{"value":119,"max":119},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"All Sections","description":""},{"title":"◯ Mechanical Body","description":"It is immune to criticals from edged weapons."},{"title":"◯ Targeting &amp; Hawk Eye","description":"Stray shots cannot occur. It also can aim through skirmishes at targets on the other side."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Magitech HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Magitech's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Magitech can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."},{"title":"Head","description":""},{"title":"► Adaptive Jet/18 (25)/Willpower/Half","description":"Dragon Fortress sprays a jet of flames, ice, or lightning.\nWithin &quot;Range/Area: 2 (50m) / Shot &quot; deals to the &quot;Target: 1 area(6m Radius) / 20&quot; 2d+20 magic damage.\nThe type of damage is chosen upon usage between Fire, Water/Ice, and Lightning."},{"title":"Body &amp; Wing","description":""},{"title":"◯ Gun","description":"The Main Battery is a gun weapon that has a &quot;Range: 2 (30m)&quot; and a maximum magazine of 3. The Machine Gun is a gun weapon that has a &quot;Range: 1 (10m)&quot; and a maximum magazine of 6."},{"title":"► Reload","description":"Fully reloads the Main Battery and Machine Gun of that section."},{"title":"► Volley","description":"To use this ability, the weapon must have at least 3 bullets loaded, and 3 bullets are consumed at the same time.\nThe success value of the Accuracy check is set to 30, with the same damage as a regular attack.\nThe same Dragon Fortress may only perform one [ ► Volley] per round against the same target."},{"title":"Body","description":""},{"title":"◯ Attack Obstacle = Impossible • Impossible","description":"The Dragon Fortress's size hinders attack.\nThe Head cannot be attacked, whether melee or ranged. This effect disappears when any Body section falls to 0 HP or lower."},{"title":"◯ Stranded","description":"If the HP of all Body sections is reduced to 0 or less, the Head sections receive a -4 penalty for Evasion checks."},{"title":"Wing","description":""},{"title":"◯ Flight II","description":"All sections receive a +2 bonus to Accuracy and Evasion only for melee attacks.\nThis unique skill is lost if any Wing section is reduced to 0 or less HP."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Rare Magical Components (900G/Black White A)"},{"roll":"2 - 6","loot":"Mysterious Magitech Components (2,400G/Black White S)"},{"roll":"7 - 12","loot":"Trove of Magical Components (7,600G/Black White S)"},{"roll":"13+","loot":"Newly Discovered Magical Components (25,000G/Black White SS)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Dragon Fortress","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"H3dseu5iig7EL9s8","name":"Gardes Dorn","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:gardes-dorn","level":8,"monsterType":"Magitech","intelligence":"Servant","perception":"Mechanical","disposition":"Instructed","soulscars":0,"languages":"Magitech language","habitat":"Shallows","reputation":16,"weakness":19,"weakPoint":"Lightning damage +3 points","initiative":15,"movementSpeed":"20(Wheels)","fortitude":"11(18)","willpower":"11(18)","source":"AB, p. 112","description":"A large Magitech soldier with a Human-like upper body equipped with blades and drills mounted on a large sphere. The tower-like head section is equipped with a cannon capable of firing powerful shock waves. It is one of the Dorn series (see CR I, p. 423 or ML, p. 158), enhanced and modified for Shallow Abyss subjugation.\n\nIt supports itself with a drive sphere that can move freely in all directions, and has the capability to respond to all situations with its close-combat blade, medium-range projectile drill arm, and long-range cannon.\n\nThe Gardes Dorn's primary objective is believed to be discovering the Abyss Core and helping its accompanying Humanoid escape to the surface. Therefore, the Gardes Dorn positions itself near the Abyss Core and attacks and eliminates anyone who doesn't possess &quot;proof of alliance.&quot; If ordered by an &quot;ally,&quot; it will swiftly destroy the Abyss Core to secure an exit. Otherwise, it continues to defend the Abyss Core &quot;for allies who will come someday.&quot;","combatStyles":[{"style":"Gun Barrel (Head)","accuracy":"10(17)","damage":"2d+7","evasion":"&#32;","defense":9,"hp":{"value":8,"max":8},"mp":{"value":32,"max":32}},{"style":"Blade (Right Half)","accuracy":"10(17)","damage":"2d+8","evasion":"&#32;","defense":9,"hp":{"value":8,"max":8},"mp":{"value":32,"max":32}},{"style":"Drill (Left Half)","accuracy":"10(17)","damage":"2d+9","evasion":"&#32;","defense":9,"hp":{"value":8,"max":8},"mp":{"value":32,"max":32}},{"style":"Drive Ball (Drive Ball)","accuracy":"11(17)","damage":"2d+8","evasion":"&#32;","defense":10,"hp":{"value":10,"max":10},"mp":{"value":32,"max":32}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"All Sections","description":""},{"title":"◯Mechanical Body","description":"It is immune to criticals from edged weapons."},{"title":"◯Targeting &amp; Hawk Eye","description":"Ranged attacks and the use of any &quot;Area: Shot &quot; effect do not cause stray shots, and it can aim through shielding."},{"title":"◯Poison Immunity, ◯Disease Immunity, ◯Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Magitech HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Magitech's HP."},{"title":"◯Can Be Detected","description":"Magitech can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."},{"title":"Head","description":""},{"title":"►Shock Cannon / 10 (17) / Fortitude / Half","description":"With &quot;Range/Area: 2 (30m) / Line &quot;, releases a shockwave from the cannon, dealing 2d+8 points of Bludgeoning magic damage to the target.\nThis effect cannot be used in consecutive turns."},{"title":"Right Body","description":""},{"title":"🗨Red-hot Blade","description":"Heats the blade to a red-hot state. When this attack hits, the damage dealt becomes Fire type, and simultaneously treats the target's Defense as halved (rounded up).\nWithin a Shallow Abyss, the blade's damage type becomes Curse and Fire."},{"title":"►Blade Spin / 10 (17) / Evasion / Negates","description":"Spins the blade horizontally to slice the surroundings. Deals 2d+7 points of physical damage to &quot;Target: 1 area (3m radius) / 5&quot; with &quot;Range: Caster.&quot;\nThe effects of [🗨Red-hot Blade] also apply to this attack. This effect cannot be used if the Drive Ball section's HP is 0 or below, or if [◯Gyro Malfunction] occurs."},{"title":"Left Body","description":""},{"title":"►Drill Attack / 10 (17) / Evasion / Negates","description":"Performs a melee Drill attack on 1 enemy character, dealing 2d+9 points of physical damage. When calculating applied damage, this attack treats the target's Defense value as half (rounded up)."},{"title":"►Drill Shot &amp; Retraction / 10 (17) / Evasion / Negates","description":"Launches the arm drill at high speed to attack, then immediately retracts it using the connected chain to enable reuse.\nWith &quot;Range/Area: 2(20m) / Line &quot;, deals 2d+8 points of physical damage to the target. When calculating applied damage, this attack treats the target's Defense as half (rounded up).\nThe Left Body section that used this ability receives a -1 penalty to Evasion checks until the start of its next turn."},{"title":"Drive Ball","description":""},{"title":"◯Attack Obstacle = +4 • None","description":"Its size hinders attacks.\nHead, Right Body and Left Body sections gain a +4 bonus to Evasion checks against melee attacks.\nThis effect is lost when the Drive Ball section's HP falls to 0 or less or when [◯Gyro Malfunction] occurs."},{"title":"◯Gyro Malfunction","description":"When the Drive Ball section receives 15 or more points of Bludgeoning-type damage from a single attack, spell, item, or other effect, the entire monster falls prone. This lasts for 10 seconds (1 round), specifically until the start of the next turn of the character who caused the damage. After this time passes, it automatically recovers from the prone state without waiting for its turn.\nWhile this effect is active, this monster cannot move, loses the effects of [◯Targeting &amp; Hawk Eye] and [◯Attack Obstacle], and Right Body section cannot use [►Blade Spin]. Furthermore, all sections receive a -2 penalty to Accuracy checks, Evasion checks, and Success Values for unique skills."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Iron (20G/Black B) x 1d"},{"roll":"2 - 7","loot":"Magitech Components (300G/Black White A)"},{"roll":"8 - 10","loot":"Rare Magitech Components (900G/Black White A)"},{"roll":"11+","loot":"Mysterious Magitech Components (2,400G/Black White S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Gardes Dorn","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"HClfYwrzffdg6IyL","name":"Shushkar","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:shushkar","level":6,"monsterType":"Magitech","intelligence":"Servant","perception":"Mechanical","disposition":"Instructed","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Ruins, Wilderness, Shallows","reputation":14,"weakness":16,"weakPoint":"Wind-type damage +3 points","initiative":12,"movementSpeed":"15 (6 Legs) / 20 (Flying)","fortitude":"8(15)","willpower":"8(15)","source":"AB, p. 110","description":"Shushkar is an insect-like machine with 6 legs. With a total length of about 5m, it carries two rows of containers on its back, in which up to 8 units (4x2) of Shuiri are mounted.\n\nThis is the mother unit that carries Shuiri. The plan was to send instructions through Shushkar to control its child units to search Shallow Abysses, but ultimately it went out of control along with the mother unit and ended in failure.\n\nWhile it can mount up to 8 Shuiri units, it rarely carries a full load.\n\nThe main body is equipped with a small Gun for self-defense. While defending itself, it launches Shuiri to ram into enemies.\n\nIt apparently can find cracks in the Shallow Abysses, and occasionally emerges to the surface, causing widespread damage.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Machine Gun (Body)","accuracy":"8(15)","damage":"2d+4","evasion":"&#32;","defense":7,"hp":{"value":6,"max":6},"mp":{"value":32,"max":32}},{"style":"Feathers (Feathers)","accuracy":"8(15)","damage":"2d+6","evasion":"&#32;","defense":8,"hp":{"value":3,"max":3},"mp":{"value":32,"max":32}},{"style":"Feathers (Feathers)","accuracy":"8(15)","damage":"2d+6","evasion":"&#32;","defense":8,"hp":{"value":3,"max":3},"mp":{"value":32,"max":32}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"All Sections","description":""},{"title":"◯Poison Immunity, ◯Disease Immunity, ◯Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Magitech HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Magitech's HP."},{"title":"◯Can Be Detected","description":"Magitech can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."},{"title":"Body","description":""},{"title":"◯Gun","description":"The Machine Gun is treated as a Gun weapon with &quot;Range: 1 (10m)&quot; and max. magazine of 3."},{"title":"►Reload","description":"Fully reloads the Machine Gun's ammunition."},{"title":"◯Drone Storage","description":"This monster has 8 storage bays where Shuiri can be stored. Without scenario instructions or GM guidance, assume 1d+2 units are stored at the time of encounter."},{"title":"⏩Drone Deployment","description":"This effect can only be used once per turn.\nLaunch 1d units of stored Shuiri. If the die roll exceeds the number in storage, launch all stored units. Launched Shuiri can act immediately after deployment."},{"title":"⏩Drone Replenishment (Shallow only)","description":"This effect can only be used once per turn immediately after performing [⏩Drone Deployment] when this monster is within a Shallow Abyss.\nInstantly replenishes 1d Shuiri from the storage. If this would exceed the maximum number (8), replenish only up to the maximum."},{"title":"Feathers","description":""},{"title":"◯Aerial Standby","description":"If the Feathers section ends its turn without performing any melee attacks, all sections of this monster cannot be targeted by melee attacks for the next 10 seconds (1 round).\nThis effect is lost if any Feathers section's HP falls below 0."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Iron (20G/Black B) x 3"},{"roll":"2 - 7","loot":"Crude Magitech Components (100G/Black White A)"},{"roll":"8 - 11","loot":"Magitech Components (300G/Black White A)"},{"roll":"12+","loot":"Rare Magitech Components (900G/Black White A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Shushkar","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"HbwOza0Hyya0FgAG","name":"Barba Kagner","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:barba-kagner","level":9,"monsterType":"Magitech","intelligence":"Servant","perception":"Mechanical","disposition":"Instructed","soulscars":0,"languages":"Magitech","habitat":"Ruins","reputation":16,"weakness":19,"weakPoint":"Lightning damage +3 points","initiative":15,"movementSpeed":"10 (Wheeled)","fortitude":"12 (19)","willpower":"12 (19)","source":"CR III p. 388","description":"This is a large Kagner specialized for transporting Maris Barba and capable of storing three Maris Barba.\n\nIt was assumed that Kagner would move to the vicinity of the operation area and launch Maris Barba to attack the base, but there is no record of its actual use in battle. The number of Barba Kagner found at ruins is extremely small, and they are also known as &quot;phantom Magitechs.&quot;","combatStyles":[{"style":"Machine Gun (Right Side)","accuracy":"12 (19)","damage":"2d+9","evasion":"13 (20)","defense":7,"hp":{"value":68,"max":68},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}},{"style":"Machine Gun (Left Side)","accuracy":"12 (19)","damage":"2d+9","evasion":"13 (20)","defense":7,"hp":{"value":68,"max":68},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}},{"style":"Wheels (Cart)","accuracy":"11 (18)","damage":"2d+14","evasion":"11 (18)","defense":10,"hp":{"value":85,"max":85},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"All Sections","description":""},{"title":"◯ Mechanical Body","description":"It is immune to criticals from edged weapons."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Magitech HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Magitech's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Magitech can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."},{"title":"Right Side/Left Side","description":""},{"title":"◯ Gun","description":"The Machine Gun is treated as a gun weapon with a &quot;Range: 2 (20m)&quot; and a maximum magazine of 3."},{"title":"◯ Targeting &amp; Hawk Eye","description":"Stray shots cannot occur. It also can aim through skirmishes at targets on the other side."},{"title":"► Reload","description":"Reloads bullet into the Machine Gun."},{"title":"Cart","description":""},{"title":"► Maris Barba Launch","description":"One stored Maris Barba is launched. The launched Maris Barba appears in the same position (area, coordinate) as this monster and performs movement and actions starting next round.\nThis ability cannot be used on consecutive turns. It can be used up to 3 times."},{"title":"► Sprinkle Repair Liquid/Can't","description":"Applies Magitech restoring liquid to &quot;Target: 1 Character&quot; (including itself) with &quot;Range: Touch,&quot; and if the target is a Magitech, its HP is restored by 2d+10 points.\nThis ability cannot be used on consecutive turns."},{"title":"◯ Stranded","description":"If the HP of the Cart section becomes 0 or less, the Right Side and Left Side receive a -4 penalty on Evasion checks."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Iron (20G/Black B)"},{"roll":"2 - 8","loot":"Rare Magitech Components (900G/Black White A)"},{"roll":"9 - 12","loot":"Mysterious Magitech Components (2,400G/Black White S)"},{"roll":"13+","loot":"Trove of Magical Components (7,600G/Black White S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Barba Kagner","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"HpW9kwWoqs8Wd5g7","name":"Redorn","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:redorn","level":3,"monsterType":"Magitech","intelligence":"Servant","perception":"Mechanical","disposition":"Instructed","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Ruins","reputation":10,"weakness":13,"weakPoint":"Lightning damage + 3 points","initiative":9,"movementSpeed":"13 (Wheeled)","fortitude":"4 (11)","willpower":"4 (11)","source":"SSS, Monstrous Lore p. 159","description":"This is an improved version of Dorn with slightly improved performance. It is recorded that a small number of this model was produced as a research magitech as a basis for the development of other higher models of Dorns.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Hammer","accuracy":"5 (12)","damage":"2d+5","evasion":"4 (11)","defense":3,"hp":{"value":23,"max":23},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Mechanical Body","description":"It is immune to criticals from edged weapons."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Magitech HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Magitech's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Magitech can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Iron (20G/Black B)"},{"roll":"2 - 8","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"9+","loot":"Crude Magitech Components (100G/Black White A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Redorn","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"JBoQyxO4eJ6hGq1m","name":"Shuiri","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:shuiri","level":2,"monsterType":"Magitech","intelligence":"Servant","perception":"Mechanical","disposition":"Instructed","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Ruins, Wilderness, Shallows","reputation":10,"weakness":12,"weakPoint":"Wind type damage +3 points","initiative":10,"movementSpeed":"-/20 (Flying)","fortitude":"3 (10)","willpower":"3 (10)","source":"AB, p. 108","description":"This is a bird-type Magitech. While its appearance could be best described as a swallow with a metallic sheen, it's about the size of a crow. It was originally created to explore Shallow Abysses, designed to conduct surveys using the parent unit Shushkar as a hub.\n\nHowever, both the parent unit and these machines became corrupted by the Abyss and lost all control. These Magitech units have since become dangerous entities that indiscriminately attack anything that moves.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Slam","accuracy":"3(10)","damage":"2d+2","evasion":"&#32;","defense":3,"hp":{"value":1,"max":1},"mp":{"value":32,"max":32}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Flight I","description":"Gains a +1 bonus to Accuracy checks and Evasion checks for melee attacks."},{"title":"►Self-Destruction Special Attack / 3 (10) / Willpower / Half","description":"Self-destructs, dealing 2d+2 points of Fire magic damage to 1 character within touch range.\nUpon using this effect, its HP automatically becomes &quot;0&quot; and Shuiri is destroyed. Within a Shallow Abyss, the damage dealt becomes Curse + Fire type."},{"title":"◯Poison Immunity, ◯Disease Immunity, ◯Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Magitech HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Magitech's HP."},{"title":"◯Can Be Detected","description":"Magitech can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Iron (20G/Black B)"},{"roll":"2 - 10","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"11+","loot":"Crude Magitech Components (100G/Black White A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Shuiri","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"MTE553r0GbFgJPID","name":"Fixed Zerlay","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:fixed-zerlay","level":7,"monsterType":"Magitech","intelligence":"Servant","perception":"Mechanical","disposition":"Instructed","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Ruins","reputation":14,"weakness":17,"weakPoint":"Bludgeoning damage +3 points","initiative":13,"movementSpeed":"10 (4 Legs)","fortitude":"9 (16)","willpower":"9 (16)","source":"CR II p. 385","description":"This is a specialized gunnery model of the Zerlay series , with three optical weapons connected side by side. The legs, which serve as the model's base, have only minimum mobility and are not designed for high-speed or long-distance movement.\n\nAlthough it has a high attack power, it is limited because the simultaneous firing of all the rays causes malfunction due to heat exhaustion.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Tube (Right Launch Tube)","accuracy":"9 (16)","damage":"2d+8","evasion":"9 (16)","defense":4,"hp":{"value":60,"max":60},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}},{"style":"Tube (Center Launch Tube)","accuracy":"9 (16)","damage":"2d+8","evasion":"9 (16)","defense":4,"hp":{"value":60,"max":60},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}},{"style":"Tube (Left Launch Tube)","accuracy":"9 (16)","damage":"2d+8","evasion":"9 (16)","defense":4,"hp":{"value":60,"max":60},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"All Sections","description":""},{"title":"◯ Mana Coating (2)","description":"Reduces magic damage received by -2."},{"title":"► Light Ray/9 (16)/Willpower/Half","description":"Attacks with a huge ray of light.\nAttacks target within &quot;Range/Area: 2 (20m)/ Line &quot; and deals 2d+7 Energy magic damage.\nThis unique skill cannot be used on consecutive turns."},{"title":"◯ Targeting &amp; Hawk Eye","description":"[ ► Light Ray] fired into a skirmish cannot make stray shots and can attack targets beyond the skirmish."},{"title":"► Overcharge","description":"The next [ ► Light Ray] fired from the same section will have its damage increased by 3 points. This effect is cumulative up to 2 times (+6)."},{"title":"◯ Exhaust Heat","description":"If any section uses [ ► Light Ray], adjacent sections cannot use [ ► Light Ray] during the same turn.\nThe three sections are linked side by side, with the Center Launch Tube flanked by the Right and Left Launch Tubes."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Magitech HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Magitech's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Magitech can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Daemon-Resistant Material (40G/Gold Black B) x 3"},{"roll":"2 - 7","loot":"Crude Magitech Components (100G/Black White A)"},{"roll":"8 - 10","loot":"Magitech Components (300G/Black White A)"},{"roll":"11+","loot":"Rare Magitech Components (900G/Black White A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Fixed Zerlay","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"O08fIfz4iA5AolN8","name":"Vox Soldier","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:vox-soldier","level":5,"monsterType":"Magitech","intelligence":"High","perception":"Mechanical","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"Magitech","habitat":"Ruins","reputation":13,"weakness":16,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":12,"movementSpeed":"15 (Many Legs)","fortitude":"8 (15)","willpower":"6 (13)","source":"Natural History of Burlight p. 129","description":"Vox Soldiers are warriors among Voxes and are responsible for destroying enemies with physical attacks. They possess excellent offensive abilities, but their repair abilities are unstable. Their lower body consists of many legs, while the upper body resembles that of a human with an outer shell on its back.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Weapon","accuracy":"8 (15)","damage":"2d+6","evasion":"6 (13)","defense":7,"hp":{"value":40,"max":40},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Iron Body","description":"The Vox Soldier is immune to criticals from edged weapons."},{"title":"►Double Attack","description":"Attacks one target twice with a two-handed weapon."},{"title":"◯Repair and Regeneration","description":"If the monster's HP is 15 or less at the beginning of their turn, the GM rolls 1d.\nIf the roll is &quot;1-2,&quot; the effect of [◯Repair Malfunction] occurs.\nIf the roll is &quot;3-6,&quot; HP is restored by 10."},{"title":"◯Repair Malfunction","description":"This effect occurs automatically on a roll of 1-2 during [◯Repair and Regeneration].\nThe monster's Accuracy increases by +2, and its damage is increased by +2 as well.\nImmediately after this effect occurs, the monster loses both [◯Repair and Regeneration] and [◯Emergency Signal]."},{"title":"◯Emergency Signal","description":"This effect occurs automatically when the monster's HP falls to 0 or less. The GM rolls 1d immediately. Assuming the roll is X: after X rounds, X/3 (rounded up) Vox Guards will appear on the battlefield (e.g., if the roll is 3, 1 will appear after 3 rounds).\nRounds are counted starting with the next monster faction round. In other words, if the roll was 1, a new monster will appear on the battlefield when the monster faction's next turn starts.\nIn Simplified Combat, the new monster(s) will appear in the Rearguard area of the monster's faction. In Standard or Advanced Combat, the position is 15m from the monster that used this ability, in any direction the GM decides (generally, the farther away from the PCs the better, but if the GM thinks it is geographically possible, they may also stage a surprise attack from behind).\nThis effect will not occur in the following cases:\nIf the damage that made the monster's HP 0 or less was Lightning type.\nWhen a monster whose HP is 0 or less is in the state of [◯Repair Malfunction].\nWhen any kind of Vox is already due to appear because of [◯Emergency Signal]. In this case, even if multiple Voxes have their HPs at 0 or below at the same time, the dice are rolled only for 1 character chosen by the GM. Note that this effect can occur again after a new Vox has already appeared.\nA new Vox from this effect will not appear if the battle ends before it arrives (hence, the last monster defeated will not cause this effect)."},{"title":"◯Delicate Loot","description":"If Lightning-type damage is dealt to this monster at least once, the loot &quot;Intermediate Signal Circuit&quot; will be changed to &quot;Broken Magitech Components (50G/Black B).&quot;"},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Magitech HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Magitech's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Magitech can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Intermediate Signal Circuit (400G/Black White A)"},{"roll":"2 - 9","loot":"Crude Magitech Components (100G/Black White A)"},{"roll":"10+","loot":"Magitech Components (300G/Black White A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Vox Soldier","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"OGZYt8RTXeDL7F2r","name":"Material Dealer","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:material-dealer","level":12,"monsterType":"Magitech","intelligence":"Servant","perception":"Mechanical","disposition":"Instructed","soulscars":0,"languages":"Magitech","habitat":"Ruins","reputation":19,"weakness":22,"weakPoint":"Lightning damage +3 points","initiative":19,"movementSpeed":"20 (4 Legs)","fortitude":"15 (22)","willpower":"16 (23)","source":"CR III p. 389","description":"This is a Human-shaped Magitech on a cart that houses a large number of magispheres and material cards. From the back of the Magitech, a number of dexterous arms extend to provide entertainment in all directions, including cards and magic tricks.\n\nIt is said to have existed on the Alframe continent during the Magitech Civilization Period and was used in prosperous underground gambling establishments. In order to suppress a disturbance in an emergency, it can incapacitate the customers who caused the disturbance. Because of its elaborate structure, it is quite rare to find one left in the present age.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Card","accuracy":"15 (22)","damage":"2d+16","evasion":"14 (21)","defense":10,"hp":{"value":111,"max":111},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Card Throwing","description":"The Card attack is treated as a thrown attack with &quot;Range: 1 (10m)&quot;, and if it hits, it deals slashing physical damage. The Cards can be used as many times as it wants since they are infinitely generated and replenished."},{"title":"◯ Targeting &amp; Hawk Eye","description":"Stray shots cannot occur. It also can aim through skirmishes at targets on the other side."},{"title":"► ⏩ Evocations/15 (22)","description":"It can use [ Vorpal Weapon ], [ Critical Ray ], [ Paralyze Mist ], [ Heal Spray ], and [ Slash Field ] evocations. All Evocations are used at A rank. There is no limit to the number of cards; Material Dealer can use as many cards as needed.\nWhen used with a Major Action, the Evocation check is performed with the standard value, success value, described in the heading of this ability; when used with a Minor Action, the success value is treated as 0."},{"title":"► Frenzy Card Deal/Can't","description":"Within &quot;Range: Caster,&quot; Material Dealer makes countless cards fly up and attack &quot;Target: 1 area (6m Radius)/20&quot;, deals 2d+10 points of damage. In this case, roll 1d for each target. If the result is 1-3, slashing magic damage is dealt, and if the result is 4-6, slashing physical damage is dealt to that target.\nWhen this ability is used, it consumes 10 points of HP."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Magitech HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Magitech's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Magitech can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Play Cards (50G/White B)"},{"roll":"2 - 8","loot":"Rare Magitech Components (900G/Black White A)"},{"roll":"9 - 11","loot":"Mysterious Magitech Components (2,400G/Black White S)"},{"roll":"12+","loot":"Trove of Magical Components (7,600G/Black White S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Material Dealer","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"Sy0HvcKZ3mAaenfz","name":"Vox Guard","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:vox-guard","level":6,"monsterType":"Magitech","intelligence":"High","perception":"Mechanical","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"Magitech","habitat":"Ruins","reputation":14,"weakness":17,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":12,"movementSpeed":"15 (Many Legs)","fortitude":"9 (16)","willpower":"7 (14)","source":"Natural History of Burlight p. 129","description":"Vox Guard species are responsible for protecting other Voxes . They have excellent stability in their defensive and repair capabilities.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Weapon","accuracy":"8 (15)","damage":"2d+6","evasion":"7 (14)","defense":9,"hp":{"value":50,"max":50},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Iron Body","description":"The Vox Guard is immune to criticals from edged weapons."},{"title":"🗨△Cover I","description":"Knows the [ Cover I ] Combat Feat."},{"title":"◯Repair and Regeneration","description":"If the monster's HP is 20 or less at the beginning of its turn, its HP is restored by 20."},{"title":"◯Emergency Signal","description":"This effect occurs automatically when the monster's HP falls to 0 or less. The GM rolls 1d immediately. Assuming the roll is X: after X rounds, X/2+1 (rounded up) Vox Soldiers will appear on the battlefield (e.g., if the roll is 3, 3 will appear after 3 rounds).\nRounds are counted starting with the next monster faction round. In other words, if the roll was 1, a new monster will appear on the battlefield when the monster faction's next turn starts.\nIn Simplified Combat, the new monster(s) will appear in the Rearguard area of the monster's faction. In Standard or Advanced Combat, the position is 15m from the monster that used this ability, in any direction the GM decides (generally, the farther away from the PCs the better, but if the GM thinks it is geographically possible, they may also stage a surprise attack from behind).\nThis effect will not occur in the following cases:\nIf the damage that made the monster's HP 0 or less was Lightning type.\nWhen any kind of Vox is already due to appear because of [◯Emergency Signal]. In this case, even if multiple Voxes have their HPs at 0 or below at the same time, the dice are rolled only for 1 character chosen by the GM. Note that this effect can occur again after a new Vox has already appeared.\nA new Vox from this effect will not appear if the battle ends before it arrives (hence, the last monster defeated will not cause this effect)."},{"title":"◯Delicate Loot","description":"If Lightning-type damage is dealt to this monster at least once, the loot &quot;Intermediate Signal Circuit&quot; will be changed to &quot;Broken Magitech Components (50G/Black B).&quot;"},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Magitech HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Magitech's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Magitech can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Intermediate Signal Circuit (400G/Black White A)"},{"roll":"2 - 7","loot":"Crude Magitech Components (100G/Black White A)"},{"roll":"8 - 11","loot":"Magitech Components (300G/Black White A)"},{"roll":"12+","loot":"Rare Magitech Components (900G/Black White A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Vox Guard","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"T6d1jv9pcLYm7e0c","name":"Gavan DOOM","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:gavan-doom","level":9,"monsterType":"Magitech","intelligence":"Servant","perception":"Mechanical","disposition":"Instructed","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Wilderness, Shallows","reputation":15,"weakness":18,"weakPoint":"Lightning damage +3 points","initiative":14,"movementSpeed":"18 (4 Legs)","fortitude":"14 (21)","willpower":"11 (18)","source":"AB, p. 113","description":"This is a giant quadrupedal Magitech soldier. Standing over 3 meters tall, it is equipped with two large cannons mounted on its upper body.\n\nThe lower body has a small-caliber gun port for short-range interception on the right side, and a large shield fixed on the left side. On the left side of the body, there is a mechanism that supplies ammunition to all of this Magitech soldier's guns, which is protected by the shield (though each gun has its own backup feed mechanism, using these results in a significant decrease in fire rate).\n\nIt is believed that units produced outside the Alframe continent were swallowed by Shallow Abysses, though some have managed to escape from the Shallows and have been spotted on the surface.\n\nApparently built purely for combat, it poses a considerable threat. Moreover, due to the influence of the Shallow, it has lost its ability to discriminate and will indiscriminately attack any armed opponent. However, it has a distinctive trait of not attacking unarmed targets (though once they use magic or other forms of attack, it immediately classifies them as enemies).","combatStyles":[{"style":"Main Gun (Turret)","accuracy":"10(17)","damage":"2d+15","evasion":"&#32;","defense":11,"hp":{"value":6,"max":6},"mp":{"value":32,"max":32}},{"style":"Main Gun (Turret)","accuracy":"10(17)","damage":"2d+15","evasion":"&#32;","defense":11,"hp":{"value":6,"max":6},"mp":{"value":32,"max":32}},{"style":"Secondary Gun (Right Half)","accuracy":"12(19)","damage":"2d+10","evasion":"&#32;","defense":9,"hp":{"value":9,"max":9},"mp":{"value":32,"max":32}},{"style":"Shield (Left Half)","accuracy":"11(18)","damage":"2d+10","evasion":"&#32;","defense":10,"hp":{"value":11,"max":11},"mp":{"value":32,"max":32}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"All Sections","description":""},{"title":"◯Mechanical Body","description":"It is immune to criticals from edged weapons."},{"title":"◯Targeting &amp; Hawk Eye","description":"Ranged attacks and the use of the &quot;Area: Shot &quot; effect do not cause stray shots, and it can aim through shielding."},{"title":"◯Protective Shield Deployment","description":"When any section receives typed damage of either &quot;Earth&quot;, &quot;Water/Ice&quot;, &quot;Fire&quot;, &quot;Wind&quot;, or &quot;Light&quot; type, a defensive barrier against that type is automatically deployed targeting all sections. While the barrier is deployed, no damage or effects of the corresponding type will be received.\nWhen a new barrier is deployed, the effects of any previous barrier are lost."},{"title":"◯Poison Immunity, ◯Disease Immunity, ◯Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Magitech HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Magitech's HP."},{"title":"◯Can Be Detected","description":"Magitech can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."},{"title":"Turret &amp; Right Half","description":""},{"title":"◯Gun","description":"The Main Gun is treated as a Gun weapon with &quot;Range: 2 (30m)&quot; and Max. Magazine of 1, while the Secondary Gun has &quot;Range: 1 (10m)&quot; with Max. Magazine count 3."},{"title":"►Reload","description":"Only reloads weapons in its own section, completely replenishing ammunition. Cannot be performed while Left Body section is operational."},{"title":"Right Half &amp; Left Half","description":""},{"title":"◯Attack Obstacle = Impossible • None","description":"Size prevents attacks.\nTurret section cannot be targeted by melee attacks.\nThis effect is lost if either Right Half or Left Half section's HP falls to 0 or below."},{"title":"Right Half","description":""},{"title":"►Burst Shot / 14 (21) / Evasion / Negates","description":"This effect cannot be used unless the Secondary Gun has 3 bullets fully reloaded. When this effect is used, it consumes all 3 bullets. Performs a &quot;Range/Area: (10m) / Shot &quot; attack that deals 2d+12 points of magical damage to &quot;Target: 1 Character.&quot;"},{"title":"Left Half","description":""},{"title":"►Reload","description":"Completely reloads ammunition for weapons in all sections."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Iron Ingot (100G/Black B)"},{"roll":"2 - 8","loot":"Rare Magitech Components (900G/Black White A)"},{"roll":"9+","loot":"Mysterious Magitech Components (2,400G/Black White S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Gavan DOOM","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"U2GAu6EF9JHUluK4","name":"Kagner","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:kagner","level":3,"monsterType":"Magitech","intelligence":"Servant","perception":"Mechanical","disposition":"Instructed","soulscars":0,"languages":"Magitech","habitat":"Ruins","reputation":10,"weakness":13,"weakPoint":"Lightning damage +3 points","initiative":9,"movementSpeed":"10(Wheeled)","fortitude":"5 (12)","willpower":"5 (12)","source":"CR III p. 384","description":"This is a transportation Magitech used to carry Magitechs during the Magitech Civilization Period in the Alfleim region. It is about 1m high and 3m long with wheels.\n\nThe pedestal has fasteners and fixations for mooring another Magitech, making it suitable for long-distance transportation. It was capable of moving by itself and being towed by a train to carry the Magitech in succession.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Slam","accuracy":"4 (11)","damage":"2d+4","evasion":"4 (11)","defense":4,"hp":{"value":28,"max":28},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Mechanical Body","description":"It is immune to criticals from edged weapons."},{"title":"◯ Mounted Magitech = 2 Characters","description":"Up to 2 Magitech characters (2 sections) can be mounted ."},{"title":"◯ Mounted Person Protection = +2 • None","description":"A character mounted on this monster has a +2 bonus to Evasion checks against melee attacks."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Magitech HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Magitech's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Magitech can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Iron (20G/Black B)"},{"roll":"2 - 7","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"8+","loot":"Crude Magitech Components (100G/Black White A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Kagner","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"VQi6XaU7TY9vG3n4","name":"Barba","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:barba","level":4,"monsterType":"Magitech","intelligence":"Servant","perception":"Mechanical","disposition":"Instructed","soulscars":0,"languages":"Magitech","habitat":"Ruins, Mountains","reputation":11,"weakness":14,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":11,"movementSpeed":"-/10(Floating)","fortitude":"6 (13)","willpower":"5 (12)","source":"CR III p. 384","description":"During the Magitech Civilization Period, the tactic of attacking from the air to the ground in large-scale field battles and sieges was devised, and the Barba series of Magitech was developed to realize this tactic.\n\nIt looks like a spider about 50 cm in length and moves by floating with a small air sac on its back. It holds a Bursting Shell between its legs, which it drops to attack a wide area.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Legs","accuracy":"6 (13)","damage":"2d+5","evasion":"6 (13)","defense":3,"hp":{"value":31,"max":31},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"► Bursting Shell Drop/6 (13)/Willpower/ Half","description":"The bursting shell is dropped on the top of the target.\nWith &quot;Range: Caster,&quot; this attack deals 2d+5 Fire magic damage to &quot;Target: 1 area (3m Radius)/5&quot;.\nThis ability can only be used once."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Magitech HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Magitech's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Magitech can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Iron (20G/Black B)"},{"roll":"2 - 5","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"6 - 9","loot":"Crude Magitech Components (100G/Black White A)"},{"roll":"10+","loot":"Magitech Components (300G/Black White A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Barba","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"VbcQNH3BYwVMdAa0","name":"Bit","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:bit","level":1,"monsterType":"Magitech","intelligence":"Servant","perception":"Mechanical","disposition":"Instructed","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Ruins","reputation":7,"weakness":11,"weakPoint":"Bludgeoning Damage +3","initiative":7,"movementSpeed":"-/15 (Floating)","fortitude":"2 (9)","willpower":"2 (9)","source":"BM","description":"It is a small magical machine, about the size of a small bag, that also serves as an alarm beacon. Floating at low speeds, they emit a loud alarm if they detect an intruder. They come in a variety of shapes, but most are cone or triangular pyramids with a tapered end.\n\nThere are often cases where multiple Bits accompany other Magitech machines to provide support.","combatStyles":[{"style":"None","accuracy":"-","damage":"-","evasion":"3 (10)","defense":1,"hp":{"value":12,"max":12},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"► Blitz / 2 (9) / Fortitude / Half","description":"Fires an electric shock at &quot;Target: 1 Character&quot; within &quot;Range: Touch,&quot; dealing 2d-2 Lightning magic damage."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Magitech HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Magitech's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Magitech can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 10","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"11+","loot":"Old Recording Device (100G / Black White A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Bit","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"YG6n8LhktnB0v6Gk","name":"Magireplica","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:magireplica","level":2,"monsterType":"Magitech","intelligence":"Servant","perception":"Mechanical","disposition":"Instructed","soulscars":0,"languages":"Magitech","habitat":"Ruins","reputation":0,"weakness":0,"weakPoint":"Lightning damage +3 damage","initiative":0,"movementSpeed":"※ ( ※ )/ ※ ( ※ )","fortitude":"※","willpower":"※","source":"CR III p. 383","description":"The Magireplica is a Magitech modeled after an Animal. Except for the fact that it is obviously made of metal, it looks exactly like the modeled animal and behaves very similarly. Even if the animal has unique skills, they are reproduced by magitech.\n\nIn the history of Magitech development, it is said to be the result of the attempt to gain various knowledge by &quot;learning from nature,&quot; but it seems that many of them were created as a hobby.","combatStyles":[{"style":"※ ( ※ )","accuracy":"※ +1","damage":"※ +2","evasion":"※","defense":0,"hp":{"value":0,"max":0},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Mechanical Body","description":"It is immune to criticals from edged weapons."},{"title":"◯ By Model","description":"The strength of this monster depends on the modeled animal. Please apply the modeled animal monster's values to the place marked with ※ in the various values and data columns.\nIts level is equal to the Animal Monster's Level + 1. In the case of a multi-section model, the Main Section is always &quot;None&quot;.\nBasically, Magireplica has the same unique skills. However, it does not have the effect of regenerating its own HP (such as [ ◯ Regeneration] and [ ◯ Bloodsucking])."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Magitech HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Magitech's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Magitech can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Iron (20G/Black B)"},{"roll":"2 - 5","loot":"Crude Magitech Components (100G/Black White A)"},{"roll":"6 - 9","loot":"Magitech Components (300G/Black White A)"},{"roll":"10+","loot":"Rare Magitech Components (900G/Black White A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Magireplica","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"ZJ4ZEbcddX3dNQoi","name":"Railway Cannon","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:railway-cannon","level":11,"monsterType":"Magitech","intelligence":"Servant","perception":"Mechanical","disposition":"Instructed","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Plains","reputation":11,"weakness":21,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":17,"movementSpeed":"30 (Many Legs)","fortitude":"14 (21)","willpower":"14 (21)","source":"CR II p. 389","description":"This is a large self-propelled Magitech created in the Magitech Civilization Period for use as a base of invasion or defense. It is designed to move on rough roads with its legs, and on tracks with wheels used by trains for long-distance travel.\n\nIt is about the same size as a train car, but there is a record that several of them were linked and used in large-scale battles.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Cannon (Train Gun)","accuracy":"15 (22)","damage":"2d+16","evasion":"12 (19)","defense":8,"hp":{"value":80,"max":80},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}},{"style":"Cannon (Train Gun)","accuracy":"15 (22)","damage":"2d+16","evasion":"12 (19)","defense":8,"hp":{"value":80,"max":80},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}},{"style":"Leg (Base)","accuracy":"13 (20)","damage":"2d+13","evasion":"13 (20)","defense":12,"hp":{"value":100,"max":100},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}},{"style":"Leg (Base)","accuracy":"13 (20)","damage":"2d+13","evasion":"13 (20)","defense":12,"hp":{"value":100,"max":100},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"All Sections","description":""},{"title":"◯ Mechanical Body","description":"It is immune to criticals from edged weapons."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Magitech HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Magitech's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Magitech can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."},{"title":"Train Gun","description":""},{"title":"◯ Targeting","description":"Stray shots cannot occur."},{"title":"◯ Gun","description":"The Cannon is treated as a Gun weapon with a &quot;Range: 2 (50m)&quot; and a maximum magazine of 1."},{"title":"► Reload","description":"Reloads bullet into the cannon."},{"title":"⏩ △ Bursting Shell","description":"The loaded bullet is changed to attack with &quot;Target: 1 area(4m Radius) / 10&quot;. Damage and range distance remains the same.\nThis unique skill can only be used when the bullet is loaded and consumes 10 points of the section's HP."},{"title":"Base","description":""},{"title":"⏩ △ Wheel Drive","description":"This unique skill can only be used when this monster is on track. Also, it cannot be used when the HP of any Base section is less than 0.\nThe built-in wheels are lowered onto the tracks. The Railway Cannon can move on the tracks at a speed of &quot;90 (wheels)&quot;.\nIt cannot use [ ► Trampling Down] on the same turn as this unique skill."},{"title":"► Trampling Down/13 (20)/Fortitude/Half","description":"Railway Cannon stomps around the area. It deals 2d+10 earth physical damage to &quot;Target: 1 area (3m Radius)/All&quot; with &quot;Range: Caster.&quot;\nAfter this effect is used by one of the Base sections, it cannot be used by the Base section in the same round."},{"title":"► Loading Aid","description":"Selects one of the Trail Gun sections and reload the bullet into that cannon."},{"title":"◯ Attack Obstacle = +4 • +4","description":"Its size hinders attacks.\nAll Train Guns gain a +4 bonus to Evasion checks against melee and ranged attacks.\nIf the HP of any Base section falls below 0 or below, this effect is lost."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Giant Magitech Components (3,000G/Black White S)"},{"roll":"2 - 8","loot":"Rare Magitech Components (900G/Black White A)"},{"roll":"9 - 12","loot":"Mysterious Magitech Components (2,400G/Black White S)"},{"roll":"13+","loot":"Trove of Magical Components (7,600G/Black White S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Railway Cannon","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"axLMquBYLOgImGNK","name":"Hibrayzan","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:hibrayzan","level":7,"monsterType":"Magitech","intelligence":"Servant","perception":"Mechanical","disposition":"Instructed","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Ruins, Caves","reputation":14,"weakness":17,"weakPoint":"Lightning damage + 3 points","initiative":14,"movementSpeed":"-/18(Floating)","fortitude":"9 (16)","willpower":"9 (16)","source":"Monstrous Lore p. 164","description":"Hibrayzan is a Magitech soldier designed for close combat, with long arms. Its body is comprised of two spheres, one above the other and one below the other, with the head buried in the body and shaped like a plate. The blades on both arms can be heated red-hot, and the power of their slashes is fearsome.\n\nThe blade grows directly from the lower half of the body, spinning as it approaches and cleaving surrounding enemies.\n\nHibrayzans appear to be intended for operation on top of Kagners , and are often seen working together simultaneously.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Cutting Blade (Upper Body)","accuracy":"10 (17)","damage":"2d+9","evasion":"9 (16)","defense":8,"hp":{"value":55,"max":55},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}},{"style":"Rotating Blade (Lower Body)","accuracy":"9 (16)","damage":"2d+11","evasion":"10 (17)","defense":6,"hp":{"value":45,"max":45},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"All Sections","description":""},{"title":"◯ Mechanical Body","description":"It is immune to criticals from edged weapons."},{"title":"◯ Fire Immunity , ◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Magitech HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Magitech's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Magitech can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."},{"title":"Upper Body","description":""},{"title":"► Twin Strike &amp; Double Attack","description":"It can make two attacks with Cutting Blade each round, though each attack requires its own Accuracy check. They may choose to attack different characters with each attack."},{"title":"◯ Cutting Blade","description":"Any attacks with Cutting Blade treat Defense as halved (rounded up)."},{"title":"◯ Cool Blade","description":"If the Cutting Blade's HP is reduced by 1 or more points due to physical damage or magical damage of Water/Ice or Lightning type, the Cutting Torch's damage is reduced by 4 points until the end of the next turn."},{"title":"Lower Body","description":""},{"title":"◯ Painful Strike","description":"If the 2d roll of the damage roll is 10 or more, the damage is increased by an additional +5 points."},{"title":"⏩ Combat Maneuver","description":"Hibrayzan flies around in a complex trajectory while floating. The Upper Body section gains a +1 bonus to its Accuracy and Evasion checks. At the same time, Lower Body receives a -1 penalty on Accuracy and Evasion checks. This effect can be used only once per round and cannot be used in consecutive turns."},{"title":"► Rotating Blade/10 (17)/Evasion/Negates","description":"Lower Body of Hibrayzan with its blade attack targets around it.\nIt attacks with its Melee Attack up to 5 targets around it.\nThis ability cannot be used on consecutive turns."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Magitech Components (300G/Black White A)"},{"roll":"2 - 8","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"9+","loot":"Rare Magitech Components (900G/Black White A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Hibrayzan","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"bAIeoULK00BdM1A3","name":"Burrdorn","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:burrdorn","level":4,"monsterType":"Magitech","intelligence":"Servant","perception":"Mechanical","disposition":"Instructed","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Ruins","reputation":11,"weakness":14,"weakPoint":"Lightning damage +3 points","initiative":10,"movementSpeed":"14 (Wheels)","fortitude":"6 (13)","willpower":"6 (13)","source":"CR I p. 424","description":"This is a larger version of the Dorn , with a shooting mechanism on both hammers, which allows them to attack an opponent at a distance.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Hammer (Right Side)","accuracy":"6 (13)","damage":"2d+6","evasion":"5 (12)","defense":4,"hp":{"value":32,"max":32},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}},{"style":"Hammer (Left Side)","accuracy":"6 (13)","damage":"2d+6","evasion":"5 (12)","defense":4,"hp":{"value":32,"max":32},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"All Sections","description":""},{"title":"◯ Mechanical Body","description":"It is immune to criticals from edged weapons."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Magitech HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Magitech's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Magitech can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."},{"title":"► Hammer Throw &amp; Pull Back/5 (12)/Evasion/Negates","description":"It can throw a hammer and immediately pull it back.\nWith &quot;Target: 1 Character&quot; and &quot;Range/Area: 1 (10m)/ Shot &quot; deals 2d+4 physical damage.\nThe section that uses this ability takes a -1 penalty to its Evasion check until the beginning of its next turn."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Iron (20G/Black B)"},{"roll":"2 - 5","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"6 - 9","loot":"Crude Magitech Components (100G/Black White A)"},{"roll":"10+","loot":"Magitech Components (300G/Black White A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Burrdorn","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"dL6M85MtBCV05FaM","name":"Beep ARC","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:beep-arc","level":4,"monsterType":"Magitech","intelligence":"Servant","perception":"Magitech","disposition":"Instructed","soulscars":0,"languages":"Magitech","habitat":"Ruins","reputation":12,"weakness":14,"weakPoint":"Water/Ice Damage +3","initiative":11,"movementSpeed":"12","fortitude":"6 (13)","willpower":"6 (13)","source":"CO","description":"This Magitech is a guard for important places and objects, shaped like a humanoid with a series of small and large cylindrical cans awkwardly interlinked together.\n\nIf anything approaches the place or thing it is guarding, it warns in Magitech, and if the warning is not heeded, it will attack to subdue it.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Weapon","accuracy":"6 (13)","damage":"2d+2","evasion":"5 (12)","defense":4,"hp":{"value":32,"max":32},"mp":{"value":10,"max":10}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"⏩ Shock Baton","description":"For 10 seconds (1 round), attacks are treated as Lightning magical weapon attacks and deal +4 damage.\nWhile this skill is active, a Death Check made by any character reduced to 0 or lower HP by a weapon attack from the Beep ARC will not fail, except if double 1s are rolled.\nUsing this ability consumes 2 points of MP."},{"title":"◯ Low Power Operation","description":"If the Beep ARC's MP becomes 0, both its Accuracy and Evasion receive a -2 penalty."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Magitech HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Magitech's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Magitech can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Iron (20G / Black B)"},{"roll":"2 - 5","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"6 - 9","loot":"Crude Magitech Components (100G / Black White A)"},{"roll":"10+","loot":"Magitech Components (300G / Black White A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Beep ARC","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"ddy7APyhE9OQ3pvM","name":"Lang Kagner","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:lang-kagner","level":7,"monsterType":"Magitech","intelligence":"Servant","perception":"Mechanical","disposition":"Instructed","soulscars":0,"languages":"Magitech","habitat":"Ruins, Mountains","reputation":14,"weakness":17,"weakPoint":"Lightning damage +3 points","initiative":13,"movementSpeed":"10(Wheeled)/15(Floating)","fortitude":"10 (17)","willpower":"10 (17)","source":"CR III p. 386","description":"This is the largest type in the Kagner series . It is equipped with a powerful air-blowing mechanism and is capable of floating and moving by blowing wind.\n\nIt is also equipped with a small cannon for self-defense. Connecting an air-blowing mechanism here can launch wind cannonballs to eliminate enemies. Since this mechanism cannot work for weapons and floating systems simultaneously, the weapon is operatable only when moved by wheels.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Slam","accuracy":"10 (17)","damage":"2d+11","evasion":"9 (16)","defense":7,"hp":{"value":63,"max":63},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Mechanical Body","description":"It is immune to criticals from edged weapons."},{"title":"◯ Mounted Magitech = 2 Characters","description":"Up to 2 magitech characters (2 sections) can be mounted ."},{"title":"◯ Mounted Person Protection = +2 • +2","description":"A character mounted on this monster has a +2 bonus to Evasion checks against melee and ranged attacks."},{"title":"► Gale Artillery/9 (16)/Willpower/Half","description":"Within &quot;Range/Area: 2 (20m)/ Shot &quot;, spews a gale of wind, dealing 2d+8 wind magic damage to &quot;Target: 1 Character&quot; and knocks prone.\nThis ability can be used only when this character's movement method is &quot;Wheeled&quot; (grounded)."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Magitech HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Magitech's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Magitech can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Iron (20G/Black B)"},{"roll":"2 - 8","loot":"Magitech Components (300G/Black White A)"},{"roll":"9 - 11","loot":"Rare Magitech Components (900G/Black White A)"},{"roll":"12+","loot":"Mysterious Magitech Components (2,400G/Black White S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Lang Kagner","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"dn5j2Dji4eobNBk3","name":"Cutting Torches","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:cutting-torches","level":3,"monsterType":"Magitech","intelligence":"Servant","perception":"Mechanical","disposition":"Instructed","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Ruins, Caves","reputation":10,"weakness":13,"weakPoint":"Water/Ice damage + 3 points","initiative":10,"movementSpeed":"12 (4 Legs)","fortitude":"5 (12)","willpower":"5 (12)","source":"KF","description":"This is a type of Magitech used for excavating caves and underground areas. It was designed to melt and vaporize bedrock using heated left and right blades. However, it can only be used under specific conditions and seems to have only been used in areas where urban development was active during the Magitech Civilization era.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Cutting Torch (Right Side)","accuracy":"5 (12)","damage":"2d+4","evasion":"4 (11)","defense":3,"hp":{"value":22,"max":22},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}},{"style":"Cutting Torch (Left Side)","accuracy":"5 (12)","damage":"2d+4","evasion":"4 (11)","defense":3,"hp":{"value":22,"max":22},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"All Sections","description":""},{"title":"◯ Cutting Blade","description":"Any attacks with Cutting Torch treat Defense as halved (rounded up)."},{"title":"◯ Cool Blade","description":"If the Cutting Torch's HP is reduced by 1 or more points due to physical damage or magical damage of Water/Ice or Lightning type, the Cutting Torch's damage is reduced by 4 points until the end of the next turn."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Magitech HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Magitech's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Magitech can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Iron (20G/Black B) x 2"},{"roll":"2 - 9","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"10+","loot":"Crude Magitech Components (100G/Black White A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Cutting Torches","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"i5KFwBKIQ9I1RCnt","name":"Miga","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:miga","level":5,"monsterType":"Magitech","intelligence":"Servant","perception":"Mechanical","disposition":"Instructed","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Ruins, Caves","reputation":13,"weakness":16,"weakPoint":"+2 Magic Damage","initiative":12,"movementSpeed":"15","fortitude":"8 (15)","willpower":"7 (14)","source":"Monstrous Lore p. 161","description":"Miga is a Magitech that resembles a giant Humanoid with two arms. It was developed as a general-purpose machine to accompany infantry during the Magitech Civilization Period.\n\nMiga attacks by striking repeatedly with its huge arms, but it can also shoot one arm to attack a wide area. Although Migas were often found without arms and considered to be used for work, the discovery of a complete body has overturned this assumption. Nowadays, some countries and organizations are manufacturing reconstructors.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Arms","accuracy":"7 (14)","damage":"2d+6","evasion":"6 (13)","defense":6,"hp":{"value":50,"max":50},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"► Twin Strike &amp; Double Attack","description":"It can make two Arms attacks each round, though each attack requires its own Accuracy check. They may choose to attack different characters with each attack."},{"title":"► Rocket Arm/7 (14)/Evasion/Negates","description":"Shoots with the whole arm. Deals &quot;2d+8&quot; physical damage within &quot;Range: 2 (30m)&quot; and &quot;Area: Shot &quot;.\nThis ability can only be used once. If Miga uses it, it loses [ ► Twin Strike &amp; Double Attack]. On the other hand, the ability &quot; ► Faint Arm&quot; becomes available."},{"title":"► Faint Arm/Can't","description":"The auxiliary arm is used to detect the opponent's moves, and to evade their attacks. Within &quot;Range: Touch&quot; and &quot;Target: 1 Character,&quot; Evasion checks get a -2 penalty. This effect lasts for 10 seconds (1 round).\nThis ability can be used only once per round. Also, this ability can be used only after using [ ► Rocket Arm] in combat."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Magitech HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Magitech's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Magitech can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Iron (20G/Black B)"},{"roll":"2 - 8","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"9+","loot":"Magitech Components (300G/Black White A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Miga","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"iP9XZz7qEJDbu4jB","name":"Scorpo","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:scorpo","level":6,"monsterType":"Magitech","intelligence":"Servant","perception":"Mechanical","disposition":"Instructed","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Ruins, Caves","reputation":13,"weakness":16,"weakPoint":"Lightning damage + 3","initiative":13,"movementSpeed":"20(Wheeled)","fortitude":"7 (14)","willpower":"8 (15)","source":"Monstrous Lore p. 162","description":"This Magitech looks like a humanoid torso on a pedestal. The silhouette is similar to that of Androscorpion , but the legs are wheels. It has been regarded as a Magitech that was made by Barbarous, who stole the technology of Humanoid's Magitech.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Sword (Body)","accuracy":"9 (16)","damage":"2d+7","evasion":"8 (15)","defense":5,"hp":{"value":52,"max":52},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}},{"style":"Wheels (Wheels)","accuracy":"8 (15)","damage":"2d+5","evasion":"7 (14)","defense":8,"hp":{"value":48,"max":48},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"All Sections","description":""},{"title":"◯ Mechanical Body","description":"It is immune to criticals from edged weapons."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Magitech HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Magitech's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Magitech can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."},{"title":"Body","description":""},{"title":"🗨 Power Strike I","description":"It can deal an additional 4 damage on their next attack. However, any Evasion Check made by them this turn receives a -2 penalty."},{"title":"◯ Painful Strike","description":"If the 2d roll of the damage roll is 10 or more, the damage is increased by an additional +5 points."},{"title":"Wheels","description":""},{"title":"► Stir Up/8 (15)/Fortitude/Negates","description":"The wheels are violently rubbed against the ground, and dust is blown up. Within &quot;Range: Caster,&quot; this gives &quot;Target: 1 area (Radius 6m) / All&quot; a -2 penalty on Accuracy check or Evasion check for 10 seconds (1 round).\nWhich of the penalties is applied is randomly determined for each target and each time the effect is applied. Different penalties are cumulative.\nThis ability cannot be used on consecutive turns."},{"title":"◯ Standing Upright","description":"If the HP of the Wheels is 0 or less, Body section gets a -2 penalty on Evasion checks."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Iron (20G/Black B)"},{"roll":"2 - 6","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"7+","loot":"Extravagant Weapon (500G/Black White A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Scorpo","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"jHe1iqEaIXl3hnqL","name":"Colossus: Pawn","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:colossus-pawn","level":13,"monsterType":"Magitech","intelligence":"Servant","perception":"Mechanical","disposition":"Instructed","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Various","reputation":16,"weakness":23,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":20,"movementSpeed":"40 (6 Legs)","fortitude":"17 (24)","willpower":"16 (23)","source":"CR II p. 390","description":"Colossus was a giant Magitech created on the Alframe continent during the Magitech Civilization Period. It is said to have taken various forms with unparalleled destructive power. Today, most of them are inactive and have been abandoned in multiple locations. However, it is unknown whether some of them have been destroyed and will never operate again, or whether some remain in a dormant state, programmed to start working again at any moment. A few Colossi are found in working conditions at ruins.\n\nThe ones listed here are among the smallest Colossi. They look like a human upper body mounted on a hexapod base. It is said to have been used to eliminate simple threats quickly because of its low cost (for a colossus), easy maintenance, and mobility.\n\nAlthough small for a Colossus, it is still a giant, more than 10 meters tall, and a formidable enemy.","combatStyles":[{"style":"None (Core)","accuracy":"-","damage":"-","evasion":"16 (23)","defense":10,"hp":{"value":120,"max":120},"mp":{"value":60,"max":60}},{"style":"Weapon (Arm)","accuracy":"17 (24)","damage":"2d+18","evasion":"15 (22)","defense":8,"hp":{"value":95,"max":95},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}},{"style":"Weapon (Arm)","accuracy":"17 (24)","damage":"2d+18","evasion":"15 (22)","defense":8,"hp":{"value":95,"max":95},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}},{"style":"Stomp (Leg)","accuracy":"16 (23)","damage":"2d+15","evasion":"14 (21)","defense":14,"hp":{"value":110,"max":110},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}},{"style":"Stomp (Leg)","accuracy":"16 (23)","damage":"2d+15","evasion":"14 (21)","defense":14,"hp":{"value":110,"max":110},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"All Sections","description":""},{"title":"◯ Mechanical Body","description":"It is immune to criticals from edged weapons."},{"title":"◯ Mana Coating (3)","description":"Reduces magic damage received by -3."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Magitech HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Magitech's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Magitech can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."},{"title":"Core","description":""},{"title":"► Magitech 10 Level/Magic Power 13 (20)","description":""},{"title":"◯ 🗨 Magic Aptitude","description":"They can use the Combat Feats [ Targeting ], [ Magic Convergence ], [ Magic Control ], [ Hawk Eye ], and [ Metamagic/Targets ]."},{"title":"► Light Ray/16 (23)/Willpower/Half","description":"With &quot;Range/Area: 2 (50m)/ Line ,&quot; fires a Light Ray, dealing 2d+15 Energy magic damage to targets.\nThis effect cannot be used on consecutive turns."},{"title":"Arm/Leg","description":""},{"title":"► Self-Destruction Protocol/15 (22)/Willpower/Half","description":"This unique skill is always performed if either the HP of the Core sections is 0 or lower or the HP of this section is below 30. Otherwise, it is never executed.\nIt self-destructs with &quot;Range: Caster;&quot; &quot;Target: All areas (30m Radius) / All&quot; will be damaged &quot;the section's current HP value&quot; of Bludgeoning magic damage."},{"title":"Arm","description":""},{"title":"◯ Continuous Attack","description":"If the section successfully hits a target in melee, it may make a second attack against the same target."},{"title":"🗨 Aimed Attack","description":"When attacking, the section can gain a +1 bonus to Accuracy. This ability does not affect characters equipped with metal armor."},{"title":"Leg","description":""},{"title":"◯ Stranded","description":"If the HP of any Leg section is reduced to 0 or less, the Arms section and Core section suffer a -2 penalty to their Evasion checks.\nIf the HP of all Leg sections is 0 or less, the penalty to Evasion check becomes -4."},{"title":"► Trampling Down/15 (22)/Fortitude/Half","description":"Colossus stomps around the area. It deals 2d+12 Earth physical damage to &quot;Target: 1 area (3m Radius) / All&quot; with &quot;Range: Caster.&quot;\nThis effect cannot be used by any other Leg section in the same round after it was used by any Leg section."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Colossus Red Core (5,000G/Gold Black White S)"},{"roll":"2 - 6","loot":"Rare Magitech Components (900G/Black White A)"},{"roll":"7 - 10","loot":"Mysterious Magitech Components (2,400G/Black White S)"},{"roll":"11+","loot":"Trove of Magical Components (7,600G/Black White S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Colossus: Pawn","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"jI7suDSQtq5jD33I","name":"Cuir","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:cuir","level":3,"monsterType":"Magitech","intelligence":"Servant","perception":"Mechanical","disposition":"Instructed","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Ruins, Shallows","reputation":10,"weakness":13,"weakPoint":"Water/Ice damage +3 points","initiative":10,"movementSpeed":"5(Wheels)","fortitude":"4(11)","willpower":"4(11)","source":"AB, p. 108","description":"This is a Magitech exploration unit mass-produced during the middle to late Magitech Civilization Period for exploring Shallow Abysses. It's approximately 1 meter tall with a tetrahedral-shaped body and three spherical feet on its underside. The spherical feet rotate to navigate smoothly across any rough terrain.\n\nWhile it was once mass-produced and deployed into Shallow Abysses, these units quickly became impossible to operate remotely and were abandoned. These exploration units have continued their dutiful exploration within Shallows ever since, still wandering to this day.\n\nTheir functions have been corrupted by the influence of the Abyss, and when they spot outsiders, they approach and release devastating attacks to analyze their targets. Though not particularly strong individually, they possess the ability to link with companions and quickly call for reinforcements, making them unexpectedly troublesome.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Baton","accuracy":"4(11)","damage":"2d+4","evasion":"&#32;","defense":5,"hp":{"value":4,"max":4},"mp":{"value":32,"max":32}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Mechanical Body","description":"It is immune to criticals from edged weapons."},{"title":"◯All-Terrain Movement","description":"Ignore terrain penalties up to -2 (penalties worse than -3 still apply)."},{"title":"◯Lightning Strike","description":"Baton attacks deal Lightning physical damage."},{"title":"⏩Call for Support","description":"This effect costs 5 MP to use. This effect can only be used once per monster's turn.\nSummons other Magitech for support. Immediately roll 1d to determine the result.\n1d | Effect |\n1 – 2 | 1 x Gichas appears. |\n3 – 4 | 1 new Cuir appears. |\n5 – 6 | Nothing appears. If within a Shallow Abyss, MP is not consumed. |\nThe newly appeared Magitech appears 10m away from the one who used this effect. In Simplified Combat, it appears in an adjacent area that is further toward their faction's rear. In Standard/Advanced Combat, it can appear at any coordinate 10m away in any direction, as long as the GM determines it's not unnatural or unreasonable.\nThe appeared Magitech does not take its turn in the current round, but will act from the next round."},{"title":"◯Poison Immunity, ◯Disease Immunity, ◯Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Magitech HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Magitech's HP."},{"title":"◯Can Be Detected","description":"Magitech can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Iron (20G/Black B)"},{"roll":"2 - 9","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"10+","loot":"Signal Circuit (100G/Black White A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Cuir","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"jXIuSi9GCocu2BhI","name":"Skyship","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:skyship","level":14,"monsterType":"Magitech","intelligence":"None","perception":"Magic","disposition":"Instructed","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Unknown","reputation":16,"weakness":19,"weakPoint":"Fire damage +3 points","initiative":19,"movementSpeed":"-/50 (Flying)","fortitude":"18 (25)","willpower":"17 (24)","source":"CR III p. 390","description":"It is a small airship. It has no combat capability and is for transportation only. It can accommodate up to 10 passengers in addition to a pilot. Rarely excavated from the ruins of Magitech Civilization, they are sold at high prices. Some of them have sails and use wind power.\n\nThe Magitech spell [ Skyship ] can make one with the same capabilities.","combatStyles":[{"style":"None","accuracy":"-","damage":"-","evasion":"15 (22)","defense":20,"hp":{"value":200,"max":200},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Flight","description":"A Skyship receives a +1 bonus to Accuracy and Evasion only for melee attacks."},{"title":"◯ Mounted = 10 Characters","description":"Up to 10 characters can be mounted in addition to the pilot.\nThis ability can exceptionally mount characters that can store something within them to be boarded. However, characters with the [ ◯ Mounted] unique skill cannot be mounted."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Magitech HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Magitech's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Magitech can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Broken Magitech Components (50G/Black B) x 5"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Skyship","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"l9eJHmblBjSsOjGc","name":"Insaid Barba","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:insaid-barba","level":5,"monsterType":"Magitech","intelligence":"Servant","perception":"Mechanical","disposition":"Instructed","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Ruins","reputation":12,"weakness":15,"weakPoint":"Physical Damage +2","initiative":12,"movementSpeed":"-/12 (Floating)","fortitude":"7 (14)","willpower":"6 (13)","source":"GR, Battle Mastery p. 136","description":"It is a custom model of Barba with the ability to hold explosive bullets removed and replaced with a laser blade that emits high heat and a drop tank to increase overall output.\n\nIts operating time is short when running at full power, and parts of the machine itself seem to frequently break down.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Laser Blade","accuracy":"7 (14)","damage":"2d+5","evasion":"7 (14)","defense":5,"hp":{"value":64,"max":64},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Laser Blade","description":"Attacks with the Laser Blade treat the target's Defense as being reduced by half (rounded up)."},{"title":"⏩ Tracking Function","description":"Detects enemies using multiple sensors.\nThe Insaid Barba gains a +1 bonus to Accuracy checks for 10 seconds (1 round).\nUsing this ability consumes 4 HP. This ability can only be used once a round."},{"title":"⏩ Increase Output","description":"Overloads its power output in an effort to defeat enemies, gaining +4 damage for 10 seconds (1 round).\nUsing this ability consumes 4 HP. This ability can only be used once a round."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Magitech HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Magitech's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Magitech can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Iron (20G / Black B)"},{"roll":"2 - 5","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"6 - 9","loot":"Crude Magitech Components (100G / Black White A)"},{"roll":"10+","loot":"Magitech Components (300G / Black White A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Insaid Barba","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"lNRg6lbJEeySv59s","name":"Star Sniper","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:star-sniper","level":8,"monsterType":"Magitech","intelligence":"Servant","perception":"Mechanical","disposition":"Instructed","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Ruins, Plains","reputation":15,"weakness":18,"weakPoint":"Lightning damage +3 points","initiative":16,"movementSpeed":"10 (4 Legs)","fortitude":"11 (18)","willpower":"11 (18)","source":"CR II p. 386","description":"This is a Magitech for sieges, boasting an ultra-long-range weapon. While guns are the standard for such Magitechs, this is a rare type that attacks by shooting heavy javelins. The accuracy and power of the javelin, the primary weapon of the Magitech, were the highest priority in its design, and its other abilities, including mobility, were relatively low.\n\nDifferent Star Snipers variations change what is ejected into rocks, flame projectiles, etc.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Javelin","accuracy":"12 (19)","damage":"2d+15","evasion":"9 (16)","defense":4,"hp":{"value":67,"max":67},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Javelin","description":"A Javelin attack is treated as a Thrown Attack with &quot;Range: 2 (100m)&quot;.\nStar Sniper has 2d Javelins at the start of combat."},{"title":"◯ Targeting &amp; Hawk Eye","description":"It can throw Javelins into a skirmish without causing stray shots, and attack targets beyond the skirmish as well."},{"title":"► Snipe Preparation","description":"Prepares to shoot the target.\nWith &quot;Range/Area: 2 (100m) / Target ,&quot; the monster declares the next ranged attack to be performed on &quot;Target: 1 Character&quot;.\nIf this monster makes a ranged attack with a Javelin at the declared target on the next Major Action, it gains a +2 bonus to its Accuracy check and +15 points to its damage. Regardless of whether this action is made or not, and regardless of whether the attack hits or not, the effect of this ability is lost once the following Major Action is completed."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Magitech HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Magitech's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Magitech can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Iron (20G/Black B)"},{"roll":"2 - 7","loot":"Magitech Components (300G/Black White A)"},{"roll":"8 - 10","loot":"Rare Magitech Components (900G/Black White A)"},{"roll":"11+","loot":"Mysterious Magitech Components (2,400G/Black White S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Star Sniper","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"livFBngr3LfWeBre","name":"Cure Kagner","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:cure-kagner","level":5,"monsterType":"Magitech","intelligence":"Servant","perception":"Mechanical","disposition":"Instructed","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Wilderness, Shallows","reputation":13,"weakness":15,"weakPoint":"Lightning damage +3 points","initiative":11,"movementSpeed":"15 (Wheels)","fortitude":"8 (15)","willpower":"7 (14)","source":"AB, p. 109","description":"This is a Magitech vehicle approximately 1m in height and 5m in length, with a total of 10 wheels on its base. It is an enhanced and improved version of the Kagner series (see CR III, p. 384 or ML, p. 159), equipped with a large container-like Block on its cargo bed and two large arms with wide operational range. It was reportedly created to search for and protect people who had been swallowed up by Shallow Abysses and gone missing.\n\nThe container-like block on the cargo bed is storage for rescued victims. The two arms are designed to fight against external threats within the Shallow Abyss while also being useful for grabbing survivors and storing them in the container. As such, the arms can extend quite far, reaching an operational range of up to 10m.\n\nHowever, the Cure Kagners, having been abandoned in the Shallow Abysses for a long time, have gone berserk and now indiscriminately capture any Humanoid they see, attempting to store them in their container. Even if they try to escape, they are repeatedly caught and returned to the container, ultimately meeting their death. The container is now filled with these deceased victims who have turned Undead , and during combat, they may also attack as enemies.\n\nThe Cure Kagner sometimes emerges above ground with its container full of Undead, causing catastrophic damage to frontier settlements.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Slam (Cargo Platform)","accuracy":"7(14)","damage":"2d+7","evasion":"&#32;","defense":6,"hp":{"value":8,"max":8},"mp":{"value":32,"max":32}},{"style":"Scissors (Arms)","accuracy":"7(14)","damage":"2d+6","evasion":"&#32;","defense":7,"hp":{"value":6,"max":6},"mp":{"value":32,"max":32}},{"style":"Slam (Cart)","accuracy":"7(14)","damage":"2d+7","evasion":"&#32;","defense":6,"hp":{"value":7,"max":7},"mp":{"value":32,"max":32}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"All Sections","description":""},{"title":"◯Mechanical Body","description":"It is immune to criticals from edged weapons."},{"title":"◯Poison Immunity, ◯Disease Immunity, ◯Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Magitech HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Magitech's HP."},{"title":"◯Can Be Detected","description":"Magitech can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."},{"title":"Cargo Platform","description":""},{"title":"◯Enemies in the Same Boat = 5 units","description":"Up to 5 other characters can be Mounted (see CR III, p. 91, ML, p. 70).\nDue to the [◯Forced Mounting] effect in Arms section, enemy faction characters may also be mounted.\nEven for enemy characters, the handling of actions and movement while in a Mounted state remains the same. Please note that a skirmish area is inevitably formed whether they remain mounted or dismount through Minor Actions."},{"title":"◯Mounted Person Protection = +2 • +2","description":"Characters Mounted on this monster receive a +2 bonus to Evasion checks against melee attacks and ranged attacks. This effect is lost when the HP of Cargo Platform section falls to 0 or less."},{"title":"Arms","description":""},{"title":"►Double Attack (Random)","description":"Makes one attack with each of its two arms. For each attack, the target is randomly determined from among hostile creatures."},{"title":"◯Long Arms","description":"Can make melee attacks with &quot;Range/Area: 1 (10m) / Target .&quot;"},{"title":"◯Forced Mounting / 7 (14) / Fortitude / Negates","description":"Forcibly loads the hit target onto its Cargo Platform section. If the target fails the Fortitude check, its position (area/coordinates) immediately becomes the same as this monster's, and it becomes Mounted on the Cargo Platform section in a prone state.\nThis effect does not occur if the target is a character with multiple sections, or if there are already 5 characters Mounted on the Cargo Platform section."},{"title":"Cart","description":""},{"title":"◯All-Terrain Vehicle","description":"All sections ignore terrain penalty modifiers up to &quot;-2&quot; (modifiers worse than &quot;-3&quot; still apply).\nIf the Cart section's HP falls to 0 or below, this ability is lost."},{"title":"◯Attack Obstacle = +4 • None","description":"Its size hinders attacks. Cargo Platform and Arms sections, and all characters Mounted on the Cargo Platform section gain a +4 bonus to Evasion checks against melee attacks.\nIf the Cart section's HP falls to 0 or below, this ability is lost."},{"title":"◯Forceful Advance","description":"This monster ignores movement blocking and can leave skirmish areas without needing to prepare for withdrawal.\nIf the Cart section's HP falls to 0 or below, this ability is lost."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Iron (20G/Black B) x 3"},{"roll":"Always","loot":"Magitech Components (300G/Black White A)"},{"roll":"2 - 9","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"10+","loot":"Artifacts of the Dead (500G/White A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Cure Kagner","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"lqaVjW1oGl4kfc06","name":"Rock Pestle","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:rock-pestle","level":11,"monsterType":"Magitech","intelligence":"Servant","perception":"Mechanical","disposition":"Instructed","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Ruins, Caves","reputation":18,"weakness":21,"weakPoint":"Lightning damage +3 points","initiative":17,"movementSpeed":"10 (Wheels) / 10 (Swimming)","fortitude":"14 (21)","willpower":"14 (21)","source":"Natural History of Dorden p. 129","description":"This is a large Magitech, about 4-5 meters in total length. It has a shape with numerous wheels attached under a body that resembles a prone rectangular prism. At the front of the body, a massive cylindrical drilling machine extends forward, with thin multi-jointed arms extending on either side.\n\nIt is believed to be a Magitech for drilling tunnels for magic-powered trains, including the Underfang Tunnel in the Dorden region. It has high durability and can operate continuously for long periods by cooling its drill, which heats up during drilling, with its own cooling water. However, it is said that it was not used for anything other than large tunnel drilling due to its poor maneuverability.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Excavator (Body)","accuracy":"14 (21)","damage":"2d+14","evasion":"13 (20)","defense":10,"hp":{"value":110,"max":110},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}},{"style":"Arm (Right Arm)","accuracy":"15 (22)","damage":"2d+17","evasion":"14 (21)","defense":9,"hp":{"value":90,"max":90},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}},{"style":"Arm (Left Arm)","accuracy":"15 (22)","damage":"2d+17","evasion":"14 (21)","defense":9,"hp":{"value":90,"max":90},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}},{"style":"None (Base)","accuracy":"-","damage":"-","evasion":"12 (19)","defense":12,"hp":{"value":120,"max":120},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"All Sections","description":""},{"title":"◯ Mechanical Body","description":"It is immune to criticals from edged weapons."},{"title":"◯Attitude Control/Water Adaptation","description":"It will not fall prone regardless of any effects received. Additionally, if its feet are submerged in water, it ignores all penalty modifiers for &quot;unstable footing&quot; and gains a +1 bonus to Evasion for all sections."},{"title":"◯Delicate Loot","description":"When the HP of the Body section becomes 0 or less, if the HP of either or both the Right Arm and Left Arm sections is 1 or more, it loses &quot;Explosive Rounds in Production&quot; as loot equal to the number of applicable sections."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Magitech HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Magitech's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Magitech can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."},{"title":"Body","description":""},{"title":"⏩Blade Generation","description":"Using internal mana, countless small protruding blades are generated across the entire excavator. Attacks made by an excavator with this effect calculate the target's Defense as half (rounded up).\nThis effect is lost after 3 minutes (18 rounds) have passed, when the excavator deals 1 or more points of applied damage, or when the [►Blade Scatter Explosion] ability is used.\nThis ability can only be used once per round. Additionally, each time this ability is used, the Body section receives 5 points of fixed damage."},{"title":"►Blade Scatter Explosion / 15 (22) / Evasion check / Negates","description":"Scatters the generated blades as if they were exploding, attacking everything in the surroundings. Targets within &quot;Range: Caster&quot; in &quot;1 area (6m radius/All)&quot; receive 2d+10 points of physical damage."},{"title":"Right Arm / Left Arm","description":""},{"title":"🗨Decoy Attack I","description":"Can use [ Decoy Attack I ] Combat Feat."},{"title":"►Explosive Projectile Throw / 14 (21) / Willpower / Half","description":"Throw stored explosives as a thrown weapon. Within &quot;Range/Area: 2(20m) / [| Shot],&quot; deals 2d+10 points of Fire magic damage to targets in &quot;1 area (3m radius) / 5&quot;.\nThis ability can only be used once for each Right Arm and Left Arm section. Additionally, if any section uses this ability, other sections cannot use it."},{"title":"Base","description":""},{"title":"►Coolant Spray/Can't","description":"Sprays liquid around to cool the excavator. Within &quot;Range: Caster&quot; and &quot;1 Area (6m radius)/Space&quot;, the area is treated as knee-deep in water (action checks -1) for 10 seconds (1 round).\nThis ability cannot be used in consecutive turns.\nIf this ability causes water to submerge its own feet, it satisfies the conditions for the evasion bonus of the unique skill [◯Attitude Control/Water Adaptation]."},{"title":"◯Attack Obstacle = +4 • +4","description":"Size hinders attacks. The Body section gains a +4 bonus modifier to Evasion against melee and ranged attacks.\nThis effect is lost when the HP of the Base section reaches 0 or below."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Explosive Rounds in Production (2,200G/Black White S) x 2"},{"roll":"2 - 5","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"6 - 11","loot":"Rare Magitech Parts (900G/Black White A)"},{"roll":"12+","loot":"Trove of Magical Components (7,600G/Black White S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Rock Pestle","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"nEPwfE65WIxLpzoi","name":"Zerlay","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:zerlay","level":3,"monsterType":"Magitech","intelligence":"Servant","perception":"Mechanical","disposition":"Instructed","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Ruins","reputation":10,"weakness":13,"weakPoint":"Bludgeoning type damage +3 points","initiative":9,"movementSpeed":"10","fortitude":"5 (12)","willpower":"5 (12)","source":"CR I p. 423","description":"This is a Magitech often found on the Alframe continent. It has a slender Humanoid form, but it carries a launcher on its back, and when attacking, it leans forward and shoots a light projectile. Once used, the light projectile needs to be refilled with mana and cannot be fired in rapid succession. It is also characterized by the use of a special material that is inferior in hardness but superior in resistance to magic.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Slam","accuracy":"4 (11)","damage":"2d+3","evasion":"4 (11)","defense":3,"hp":{"value":25,"max":25},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Mana Coating (1)","description":"Reduces magic damage received by 1."},{"title":"► Light Bullet/5 (12)/Willpower/Half","description":"It leans forward and shoots a light projectile from its launcher. This ability can only be used with a Limited Move.\nIt cannot be used in consecutive turns. With &quot;Target: 1 Character&quot; and &quot;Range/Area: 2 (20m)/ Shot &quot;, this attack deals 2d+3 Energy magic damage."},{"title":"◯ Targeting","description":"[ ► Light Bullet] fired into a skirmish cannot stray."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Magitech HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Magitech's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Magitech can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Daemon-Resistant Material (40G/Gold Black B)"},{"roll":"2 - 8","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"9+","loot":"Crude Magitech Components (100G/Black White A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Zerlay","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"pZBscNs20lB2lbWR","name":"Zerlay Dorn","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:zerlay-dorn","level":10,"monsterType":"Magitech","intelligence":"Servant","perception":"Mechanical","disposition":"Instructed","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Ruins","reputation":17,"weakness":20,"weakPoint":"Lightning damage +3 points","initiative":16,"movementSpeed":"20 (Wheels)","fortitude":"13 (20)","willpower":"13 (20)","source":"CR II p. 388","description":"This prototype results from a project to integrate the Dorn and Zerlay series. Researchers who had been developing each other's products provided their development records to each other.\n\nIntegrating different concepts and designs was pretty challenging, but they overcame the difficulties and completed a product with a high level of combat power. Although it can be said that most of the development objectives have been achieved, there is a record that the developers lamented the gap between their actual efforts and project goals.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Tube (Right Body)","accuracy":"13 (20)","damage":"2d+12","evasion":"12 (19)","defense":9,"hp":{"value":85,"max":85},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}},{"style":"Tube (Left Body)","accuracy":"13 (20)","damage":"2d+12","evasion":"12 (19)","defense":9,"hp":{"value":85,"max":85},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}},{"style":"Hammer (Right Leg)","accuracy":"14 (21)","damage":"2d+15","evasion":"11 (18)","defense":11,"hp":{"value":95,"max":95},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}},{"style":"Hammer (Left Leg)","accuracy":"14 (21)","damage":"2d+15","evasion":"11 (18)","defense":11,"hp":{"value":95,"max":95},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"All Sections","description":""},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Magitech HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Magitech's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Magitech can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."},{"title":"Right Body/Left Body","description":""},{"title":"◯ Mana Coating (2)","description":"Reduces magic damage received by -2."},{"title":"► Light Ray/13 (20)/Willpower/Half","description":"Attacks with a huge ray of light.\nAttacks target within &quot;Range/Area: 2 (20m)/ Line &quot; and deals 2d+10 Energy magic damage.\nThis unique skill cannot be used on consecutive turns."},{"title":"◯ Targeting &amp; Hawk Eye","description":"[ ► Light Ray] fired into a skirmish cannot stray and can also attack through the skirmish at targets on the far side."},{"title":"Right Leg/Left Leg","description":""},{"title":"◯ Mechanical Body","description":"It is immune to criticals from edged weapons."},{"title":"► Hammer Throw &amp; Pull Back/12 (19)/Evasion/Negates","description":"It can throw a hammer and immediately pull it back.\nWith &quot;Target: 1 Character&quot; and &quot;Range/Area: 1 (10m)/ Shot &quot; deals 2d+13 physical damage.\nThe section that uses this ability takes a -1 penalty to its Evasion check until the beginning of its next turn."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Iron (20G/Black B) x 2"},{"roll":"Always","loot":"Daemon-Resistant Material (40G/Gold Black B) x 2"},{"roll":"2 - 12","loot":"Rare Magitech Components (900G/Black White A)"},{"roll":"13+","loot":"Trove of Magical Components (7,600G/Black White S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Zerlay Dorn","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"pfZMHM2dJsELa96t","name":"Rail Eater","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:rail-eater","level":8,"monsterType":"Magitech","intelligence":"Servant","perception":"Mechanical","disposition":"Instructed","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Ruins","reputation":15,"weakness":18,"weakPoint":"Lightning damage +3 points","initiative":14,"movementSpeed":"16 (4 Legs)","fortitude":"10 (17)","willpower":"10 (17)","source":"Natural History of Dorden p. 129","description":"These Magitech soldiers were believed to have been created by some country in the Dorden region to destroy railway tracks during a war in the late Magitech Civilization Period.\n\nThey have a four-legged, vase-like shape, move in groups, and remove railway rails. The vase-shaped body is about 150cm tall with a diameter of about 1m, and from near the rim, thin and long cutting blades extend from jointed arms that can be folded into an area. The four legs are short and thick, made of metal, supporting the body (the vase) like a base.\n\nThe inside of the vase is a high-temperature furnace for melting iron. It uses this heat to cut the rails into appropriate lengths and carries them away. Then, it melts the iron and brings it back to its base.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Fusing Blade","accuracy":"10 (17)","damage":"2d+7","evasion":"9 (16)","defense":8,"hp":{"value":58,"max":58},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Fire Immunity, ◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯Mechanical Body","description":"It is immune to criticals from edged weapons."},{"title":"◯Cutting Blade","description":"Any attacks with Fusing Blade treat Defense as halved (rounded up)."},{"title":"◯Cool Blade","description":"If the Rail Eater's HP is reduced by 1 or more points due to physical or magical damage of Water/Ice or Lightning type, the Fusing Blade's damage is reduced by 4 points until the end of the next turn."},{"title":"►Molten Iron Bullet / 10 (17) / Fortitude / Half","description":"Ejects a mass of molten iron from the top of its head like a bullet and attacks. Within &quot;Range: 1(10m)/Shot&quot; to deal &quot;2d+7&quot; points of Fire magic damage to targets in &quot;1 area (3m radius)/5.&quot;\nThis action cannot be performed in consecutive turns."},{"title":"◯Delicate Loot","description":"If HP falls to 0 or less while the [◯Cool Blade] effect is active, the &quot;Small Blast Furnace&quot; loot is lost."},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Magitech HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Magitech's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Magitech can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Small Blast Furnace (1,200G/Black White A)"},{"roll":"Always","loot":"Magitech Components (300G/Black White A)"},{"roll":"2 - 10","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"11+","loot":"Rare Magitech Parts (900G/Black White A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Rail Eater","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"rX4zNPza51gKr3yG","name":"SZerlay","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:szerlay","level":5,"monsterType":"Magitech","intelligence":"Servant","perception":"Mechanical","disposition":"Instructed","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Ruins","reputation":12,"weakness":15,"weakPoint":"Bludgeoning type damage +3 points","initiative":11,"movementSpeed":"10 (4 legs)","fortitude":"7 (14)","willpower":"7 (14)","source":"CR I p. 425","description":"This is one of the larger Magitech Zerlay series, carrying a larger launcher on its back. The larger size allows it to shoot as a light beam. It is also able to move while maintaining its posture when shooting the light beam.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Tube (Launch Tube)","accuracy":"7 (14)","damage":"2d+4","evasion":"7 (14)","defense":3,"hp":{"value":30,"max":30},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}},{"style":"Slam (Body)","accuracy":"7 (14)","damage":"2d+6","evasion":"7 (14)","defense":4,"hp":{"value":40,"max":40},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"All Sections","description":""},{"title":"◯ Mana Coating (1)","description":"Reduces magic damage received by 1."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Magitech HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Magitech's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Magitech can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."},{"title":"Launch Tube","description":""},{"title":"► Light Ray/7 (14)/Willpower/Half","description":"Attacks with a huge ray of light.\nAttacks target within &quot;Range/Area: 2 (20m)/Line&quot; and deal 2d+5 energy magic damage.\nThis unique skill cannot be used on consecutive turns."},{"title":"◯ Targeting &amp; Hawk Eye","description":"[ ► Light Ray] fired into a skirmish cannot have stray shots, and can attack targets beyond the skirmish."},{"title":"Body","description":""},{"title":"◯ Attack Obstacle = +4 • None","description":"SZerlay's height prevents enemies from attacking it. The Launch Tube receives a +4 bonus to Evasion checks against melee attacks.\nWhen the Body falls to 0 HP or lower, this effect disappears."},{"title":"◯ Loss of Mobility","description":"When the Body section HP becomes 0 or less, SZerlay cannot move."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Daemon-Resistant Material (40G/Gold Black B)"},{"roll":"2 - 5","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"6 - 8","loot":"Crude Magitech Components (100G/Black White A)"},{"roll":"9+","loot":"Magitech Components (300G/Black White A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"SZerlay","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"rahVXALCGD4OEM69","name":"Colossus: Knight","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:colossus-knight","level":16,"monsterType":"Magitech","intelligence":"Servant","perception":"Mechanical","disposition":"Instructed","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Various","reputation":19,"weakness":26,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":23,"movementSpeed":"50 (4 Legs)","fortitude":"21 (28)","willpower":"20 (27)","source":"Monstrous Lore p. 173","description":"This is a Colossus, a figure that is relatively small figuratively speaking, although its overall height is over 10 meters. Designed for mobility, it has a warrior-like appearance of a Centaur, with a horse-like lower body and an armed humanoid upper body.\n\nIts main role was to forcefully trample armies and break enemy formations with its long spears and rushing power. Equipped with destructive ray weapons, it was difficult to approach even from close range.\n\nThe Colossus may roam the wilderness or deserts in search of enemies, but it is reported to ignore only small numbers of opponents. It may be sleeping in ruins, attacking those who enter. When it awakens, it heads straight for its destination, causing serious damage to settlements and towns along the way.\n\nSome Colossi were defective, or the hangars were targeted by the Barbarous, and if found in ruins, Colossi should be neutralized or destroyed as soon as possible. However, there have been past tragedies where people have awakened them by trying to destroy them, and now Knights still roam the surrounding lands.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Spear (Right Upper Body)","accuracy":"20 (27)","damage":"2d+24","evasion":"19 (26)","defense":15,"hp":{"value":140,"max":140},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}},{"style":"Spear (Lower Upper Body)","accuracy":"20 (27)","damage":"2d+24","evasion":"19 (26)","defense":15,"hp":{"value":140,"max":140},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}},{"style":"Hooves (Front Lower Body)","accuracy":"18 (25)","damage":"2d+28","evasion":"18 (25)","defense":18,"hp":{"value":160,"max":160},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}},{"style":"Hooves (Rear Lower Body)","accuracy":"18 (25)","damage":"2d+28","evasion":"18 (25)","defense":18,"hp":{"value":160,"max":160},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"All Sections","description":""},{"title":"◯ Mechanical Body","description":"It is immune to criticals from edged weapons."},{"title":"◯ Mana Coating (4)","description":"Reduces magic damage received by -4."},{"title":"► Colossus Trample","description":"Colossus: Knight attacks with &quot;Area: Breakthrough &quot;.\nAll targets within range will be hit with Colossus: Knight, one of the sections' Melee Attacks. All section Accuracy checks gain a +2 bonus, and damage is increased by +6."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Magitech HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Magitech's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Magitech can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."},{"title":"Right Upper Body/Left Upper Body","description":""},{"title":"► Twin Strike &amp; Double Attack","description":"It can make two Spear attacks each round, though each attack requires its own Accuracy check. They may choose to attack different characters with each attack."},{"title":"Front Lower Body/Rear Lower Body","description":""},{"title":"◯ Stranded","description":"If the HP of the Front Lower Body or Rear Lower Body section is 0 or less, Right Upper Body and Left Upper Body sections suffer a -2 penalty on the Evasion check.\nIf both of them have 0 or less HP, the penalty is -4."},{"title":"Front Lower Body","description":""},{"title":"► Eradicating Ray/19 (26)/Fortitude/Half","description":"The Front Lower Body fires ray of light at &quot;Range/Area: 2 (50m)/ Line &quot;, dealing 2d+20 Energy magic damage.\nThis unique skill cannot be used on consecutive turns."},{"title":"Rear Lower Body","description":""},{"title":"► Emergency Maintenance","description":"It restores its own body. This effect restores the HP of one of the sections by 2dx5 points.\nThis effect cannot be used on consecutive turns."},{"title":"► Smoke Cover","description":"The monster creates a cloud of smoke around it, making it difficult to see. For 10 seconds (1 round), the monster's Evasion, Fortitude, and Willpower checks for all sections of this monster are increased by +2 against characters who are in another area (Simplified Combat) or 10m or more away (Standard Combat, Advanced Combat) from Colossus: Knight."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Colossus Blue Core (8,000G/Gold Black White S)"},{"roll":"2 - 8","loot":"Mysterious Magitech Components (2,400G/Black White S)"},{"roll":"9+","loot":"Trove of Magical Components (7,600G/Black White S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Colossus: Knight","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"rkASluLAPKg0jzUB","name":"Eltrias","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:eltrias","level":9,"monsterType":"Magitech","intelligence":"Servant","perception":"Mechanical","disposition":"Instructed","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Ruins, Caves","reputation":16,"weakness":19,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":16,"movementSpeed":"22","fortitude":"12 (19)","willpower":"12 (19)","source":"Monstrous Lore p. 167","description":"Eltrias is a humanoid-looking magitech soldier that was reportedly created at the end of the Magitech Civilization. Its appearance is reminiscent of a knight wielding a sword and shield, and it stands at nearly 5 meters tall. Eltrias was likely responsible for commanding other magitech soldiers.\n\nIn close combat, Eltrias is a skilled fighter, wielding its sword and shield with ease. Its shield is equipped with a built-in gun, allowing for combat at various distances. Eltrias can also deploy a Protective Shield from its body, suggesting it was designed to work in tandem with Barba (see p. 160). Eltrias has the ability to command other magitechs and can coordinate attacks with them.\n\nWhile originally designed as the core of an attack, Eltrias is sometimes stationed to protect a base without engaging in battle. However, some rogue units can be found wandering the wilderness, attacking enemy bases and settlements indiscriminately.","combatStyles":[{"style":"None (Head)","accuracy":"-","damage":"-","evasion":"12 (19)","defense":6,"hp":{"value":62,"max":62},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}},{"style":"Luminous Flux (Body)","accuracy":"12 (19)","damage":"2d+8","evasion":"11 (18)","defense":8,"hp":{"value":68,"max":68},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}},{"style":"1H Sword (Right Arm)","accuracy":"13 (20)","damage":"2d+14","evasion":"11 (18)","defense":6,"hp":{"value":66,"max":66},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}},{"style":"Large Shield (Left Arm)","accuracy":"11 (18)","damage":"2d+10","evasion":"10 (17)","defense":14,"hp":{"value":76,"max":76},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}},{"style":"Kick (Legs)","accuracy":"12 (19)","damage":"2d+10","evasion":"10 (17)","defense":10,"hp":{"value":70,"max":70},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"All Sections","description":""},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Magitech HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Magitech's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Magitech can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."},{"title":"Head","description":""},{"title":"► Attack Order","description":"The Eltrias instructs the surrounding machines to move precisely.\nMagitech characters within &quot;1 area (4m radius) / 10&quot; centered on Eltrias gain a +1 bonus to Accuracy checks and +2 points of damage for 10 seconds (1 round).\nThis effect cannot be used for consecutive turns."},{"title":"► Defensive Order","description":"The Eltrias directs the surrounding Magitechs to perform defensive actions.\nMagitech characters within &quot;1 area (4m radius)/10&quot; centered on Eltrias gain a bonus of +1 to Evasion and +2 points to Defense for 10 seconds (1 round).\nThis effect cannot be used on consecutive turns."},{"title":"Body","description":""},{"title":"◯ Luminous Flux","description":"Eltrias attacks with Luminous Flux are treated as Shooting Attacks with &quot;Range: 2 (30m)&quot;. And they deal magic damage."},{"title":"◯ Targeting","description":"Stray shots cannot occur."},{"title":"◯ Protective Shield Deployment","description":"When the Body section takes Fire, Water/Ice, Wind, Earth, or Lightning type damage, a protective shield forms around it, nullifying any subsequent attacks of the same element. When the defensive shield is put up, all sections are not affected by any damage or disadvantageous effect caused by the type.\nOnce a new protective shield is put up, any previous protective shield loses its effectiveness. At the beginning of the battle, the defensive layer against Fire is deployed."},{"title":"Right Arm","description":""},{"title":"🗨 Cleave I","description":"It can attack up to 3 characters with melee attacks that can be reached, but the damage will be reduced by -3."},{"title":"Left Arm","description":""},{"title":"► Shield Guard","description":"Eltrias protects itself with a large shield. Changes the target of ranged attacks on all sections of itself to the Left Arm section.\nDoes not interfere and stop attacks, spells, and unique skills targeting multiple sections."},{"title":"► Concealed Gun/12 (19)/Evasion/Negates","description":"The shield has a gun built into it which Eltrias can use to attacks suddenly.\nWithin &quot;Range/area:2 (20m)/ Shot &quot; it deals 2d+10 magic damage to &quot;Target: 1 Character&quot;. Characters who have already been chosen before as targets for this ability receive a +2 bonus on Evasion checks."},{"title":"Legs","description":""},{"title":"◯ Attack Obstacle = +4 • None","description":"An Eltrias' height prevents enemies from attacking it.\nThe Head and Body receive a +4 bonus to Evasion checks against melee attacks.\nWhen the Legs fall to 0 HP or lower, this effect disappears."},{"title":"◯ Overdraft/11 (18)/Fortitude/Negates","description":"A target hit by a Kick will fall prone. Characters may counter this effect with a Strength check (see CR I, p. 113) instead of Fortitude if they wish."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Rare Magitech Components (900G/Black White A)"},{"roll":"2 - 7","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"8+","loot":"Mysterious Magitech Components (2,400G/Black White S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Eltrias","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"sIacGocMw4ZxSbcr","name":"Gaspica","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:gaspica","level":7,"monsterType":"Magitech","intelligence":"Servant","perception":"Mechanical","disposition":"Instructed","soulscars":0,"languages":"Magitech language","habitat":"Shallows","reputation":15,"weakness":17,"weakPoint":"Bludgeoning type damage +3 points","initiative":12,"movementSpeed":"20 (4 Legs)","fortitude":"10(17)","willpower":"9(16)","source":"AB, p. 111","description":"Gaspica has a large box-shaped body supported by 4 legs, with a turret equipped with a large cannon mounted on top of the box.\n\nThe Gaspica is a Magitech unit created to rest and rescue accompanying soldiers during Shallow Abysses exploration, with its square body serving as a cramped but functional lodging facility and infirmary. The turret is equipped with a powerful cannon to repel enemies and will attack those who approach carelessly.\n\nThere are two ways to stop this Magitech. One is to destroy the body. In this case, the Magitech completely ceases to function. Even if the turret and legs remain undestroyed, they will stop working because the control center is destroyed.\n\nThe other way is to destroy both the turret and legs. If both can be destroyed, this monster loses its means of direct attack. This allows one to board the Body section and shut down this monster from within.\n\nIf the monster is stopped while preserving the body this way, the lodging facilities inside the body become available for use. Up to 6 people can safely sleep there simultaneously. When using the medical facilities, if one person capable of speaking or reading Magitech language supervises and operates the medical mechanical, 3 hours of rest provides recovery equivalent to 6 hours of sleep. Those who recover cannot gain recovery from sleep that day. The person monitoring and operating the mechanical functions doesn't need to focus solely on this task and can simultaneously perform simple tasks or keep watch outside.\n\nIf PCs can prove they are allies of the Gaspica, no combat will occur, and it can be used as a mobile lodging facility. In this case, the cannon, leg kicks, and sticky ammunition can be operated from inside. For each worker who can speak or read Magitech language, one section can be operated. If there are fewer than 3 workers, operation sections can be switched each round. Characters inside cannot be interfered with from the outside, but they also cannot directly interfere with the outside (except for certain effects that transcend space).","combatStyles":[{"style":"Cannon (Turret)","accuracy":"10(17)","damage":"2d+8","evasion":"&#32;","defense":9,"hp":{"value":9,"max":9},"mp":{"value":32,"max":32}},{"style":"None (Body)","accuracy":"-","damage":"-","evasion":"&#32;","defense":8,"hp":{"value":8,"max":8},"mp":{"value":32,"max":32}},{"style":"Kick (Legs)","accuracy":"9(16)","damage":"2d+10","evasion":"&#32;","defense":8,"hp":{"value":7,"max":7},"mp":{"value":32,"max":32}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"All Sections","description":""},{"title":"◯Mechanical Body","description":"It is immune to criticals from edged weapons."},{"title":"◯Targeting &amp; Hawk Eye","description":"Ranged attacks and the use of any &quot;Area: Shot &quot; effect do not cause stray shots, and it can aim through shielding."},{"title":"◯Poison Immunity, ◯Disease Immunity, ◯Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Magitech HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Magitech's HP."},{"title":"◯Can Be Detected","description":"Magitech can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."},{"title":"Turret &amp; Legs","description":""},{"title":"◯Loss of Attack Capability","description":"When both Turret and Legs sections HP fall to 0 or below, this monster completely ceases to function."},{"title":"Turret","description":""},{"title":"►Gun","description":"The Cannon is treated as a Gun weapon with &quot;Range: 2 (50m)&quot; and Max Magazine count of 2.\nInside a Shallow Abyss, the damage dealt becomes Curse type."},{"title":"►Reload","description":"Fully load the Cannon's ammunition."},{"title":"Body","description":""},{"title":"►Sticky Shot / Can't (Escape DC 14 / Fortitude)","description":"This effect can only target prone characters and costs 5 MP to use. When targeting a character with multiple sections, this MP cost is automatically multiplied by the number of sections.\nWith a &quot;Range/Area: 2 (20m) / Shot &quot;, applies an adhesive substance to &quot;Target: 1 Character X&quot;, fixing them to the ground. The target fixed to the ground cannot move or take Major Actions, and receives a -4 penalty to Evasion checks (this does not stack with prone status penalties).\nA character affected by this effect can attempt one Fortitude check at Target Number 14 at the start of their turn; if successful, they can break free from the adhesive substance.\nThis effect lasts for 3 minutes (18 rounds). If affected multiple times, only the duration is overwritten (see CR I, p. 172, MA, p. 74); the number of escape checks does not increase, nor does the target number increase."},{"title":"◯Control Center","description":"If the HP of Body section falls to 0 or below, this monster completely ceases to function."},{"title":"Legs","description":""},{"title":"◯All-Terrain Vehicle","description":"All sections ignore terrain penalties up to -2 (penalties worse than -3 still apply).\nThis ability is lost if the Legs section HP drops to 0 or below."},{"title":"◯Kick Away","description":"When a Kick attack hits, the target is kicked away. The target is moved to an adjacent area on the allied Rearguard (Simplified Combat) or 10m in any direction chosen by this monster (Standard/Advanced Combat), takes 10 points of falling damage, and is knocked prone."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Iron (20G/Black B) x 3"},{"roll":"2 - 8","loot":"Magitech Components (300G/Black White A)"},{"roll":"9 - 11","loot":"Rare Magitech Components (900G/Black White A)"},{"roll":"12+","loot":"Mysterious Magitech Components (2,400G/Black White S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Gaspica","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"tgUcV1wiMZSbxP5y","name":"Domsva","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:domsva","level":8,"monsterType":"Magitech","intelligence":"Servant","perception":"Mechanical","disposition":"Instructed","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Ruins, Caves","reputation":16,"weakness":19,"weakPoint":"Accuracy +1","initiative":14,"movementSpeed":"15/15 (Floating)","fortitude":"11 (18)","willpower":"10 (17)","source":"Monstrous Lore p. 166","description":"Domsva is an armored humanoid Magitech soldier, standing tall at over 3 meters. Its thick armor is an impressive sight to behold.\n\nDespite its slow and heavy appearance, it defies gravity with the ability to levitate on its legs, moving at surprising speeds. Its powerful knee kicks take advantage of its thrusting ability, allowing it to stand on water.\n\nA master of combat, it wields a two-handed greatsword with great vigor and carries a large two-handed cannon, albeit with a small number of bullets.\n\nIn the Magitech civilization, it was revered as a defender of important bases and a fierce attacker of enemy camps, boasting unparalleled combat power.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Weapon (Upper Body)","accuracy":"10 (17)","damage":"2d+12","evasion":"12 (19)","defense":9,"hp":{"value":85,"max":85},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}},{"style":"None (Body)","accuracy":"-","damage":"-","evasion":"12 (19)","defense":9,"hp":{"value":85,"max":85},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}},{"style":"Kick (Legs)","accuracy":"14 (21)","damage":"2d+15","evasion":"11 (18)","defense":11,"hp":{"value":95,"max":95},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"All Sections","description":""},{"title":"◯ Mechanical Body","description":"It is immune to criticals from edged weapons."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Magitech HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Magitech's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Magitech can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."},{"title":"Upper Body","description":""},{"title":"► Portable Cannon/12 (19)/Evasion/Negates","description":"Domsva uses its cannon and makes a Shooting Attack with &quot;Range: 2 (30m)&quot;, dealing 2d+8 points of magic damage.\nThis ability can be used only twice, regardless of success or failure."},{"title":"🗨 Cleave I","description":"It can attack up to 3 characters with melee attacks that can be reached, but the damage will be reduced by -3."},{"title":"🗨 All-Out Attack","description":"A Weapon can deal an additional 8 damage on its next attack. However, any Evasion check made by this section this turn receives a -3 penalty."},{"title":"Body","description":""},{"title":"► Condemning Flash/10 (17)/Fortitude/Negates","description":"&quot;Target: 1 Character&quot; is blinded for 10 seconds (1 round) by a dazzling flash within &quot;Range: 1 (10m)&quot;.\nIf the HP of the Body section is less than half of the maximum value (rounded up), the [ ► Condemning Flash] can be used twice with one Major Action. The second target can be chosen after the result of the first one. If the first target resists, the same target can be selected again."},{"title":"Legs","description":""},{"title":"◯ Attack Obstacle = Impossible • Impossible","description":"Its Legs hinder the attack.\nThe Body section cannot be attacked, whether melee or ranged.\nWhen the Legs fall to 0 HP or lower, this effect disappears."},{"title":"🗨 Kneeguard Bash","description":"The target is attacked with armor at the knee joint. The Legs section gains a +2 bonus to Accuracy checks but deals -4 damage less."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Magitech Components (300G/Black White A) x 3"},{"roll":"2 - 9","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"10+","loot":"Mysterious Magitech Components (2,400G/Black White S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Domsva","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"wUS6hfNTuENJJhpv","name":"Vox Queen","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:vox-queen","level":8,"monsterType":"Magitech","intelligence":"High","perception":"Mechanical","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"Magitech","habitat":"Ruins","reputation":14,"weakness":17,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":14,"movementSpeed":"15 (Many Legs)","fortitude":"11 (18)","willpower":"10 (17)","source":"Natural History of Burlight p. 130","description":"The Vox Queen is a commander who leads other Voxes at the front, in the place of the Vox Empress who lurks in the depths. She can reproduce Magitech used by an Artificer , making full use of her own Magitech mechanisms.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Gun","accuracy":"10 (17)","damage":"2d+8","evasion":"9 (16)","defense":9,"hp":{"value":70,"max":70},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Iron Body","description":"The Vox Queen is immune to criticals from edged weapons."},{"title":"►Magitech Reproduction 8 Level / Magic Power 11 (18)","description":"Casts Magitech spells up to 8th level with Magic Power 11. This uses no MP and consumes only &quot;1&quot; point of its own HP, regardless of the spell.\nCannot cast [Grenade] and [Pile Shooter] spells."},{"title":"◯Targeting","description":"Ranged Attacks or &quot;Area: Shot&quot; spells do not cause stray shots."},{"title":"►Gunfire / 11 (18) / Evasion / Negates","description":"Makes a Shooting Attack with a &quot;Gun&quot; with the following data (name, minimum strength, etc. are omitted).\nStance | Max Magazine | Accuracy | Crit Value | Extra Damage | Range |\n2H | 3 | - | ⑩ | - | 2 (40m) |"},{"title":"◯Repair and Regeneration","description":"If the monster's HP is 30 or less at the beginning of their turn, the GM rolls 1d.\nIf the roll is &quot;1,&quot; the effect of [◯Repair Malfunction] occurs.\nIf the roll is &quot;2-6,&quot; HP is restored by 15."},{"title":"◯Repair Malfunction","description":"This effect occurs automatically on a roll of 1 during [◯Repair and Regeneration].\nThe monster's Accuracy increases by +2, and its damage is increased by +2 as well.\nImmediately after this effect occurs, the monster loses both [◯Repair and Regeneration] and [◯Emergency Signal]."},{"title":"◯Emergency Signal","description":"This effect occurs automatically when the monster's HP falls to 0 or less. The GM rolls 1d immediately. Assuming the roll is X: after X rounds, 1 Vox Queen, X/2 (rounded up) Vox Guards , and X Vox Soldiers will appear on the battlefield (e.g., if the roll is 3, then after 3 rounds, 1 Queen, 2 Guards, and 3 Soldiers will appear).\nRounds are counted starting with the next monster faction round. In other words, if the roll was 1, a new monster will appear on the battlefield when the monster faction's next turn starts.\nIn Simplified Combat, the new monster(s) will appear in the Rearguard area of the monster's faction. In Standard or Advanced Combat, the position is 15m from the monster that used this ability, in any direction the GM decides (generally, the farther away from the PCs the better, but if the GM thinks it is geographically possible, they may also stage a surprise attack from behind).\nThis effect will not occur in the following cases:\nIf the damage that made the monster's HP 0 or less was Lightning type.\nWhen a monster whose HP is 0 or less is in the state of [◯Repair Malfunction].\nWhen any kind of Vox is already due to appear because of [◯Emergency Signal]. In this case, even if multiple Voxes have their HPs at 0 or below at the same time, the dice are rolled only for 1 character chosen by the GM. Note that this effect can occur again after a new Vox has already appeared.\nNew Voxes from this effect will not appear if the battle ends before they arrive (hence, the last monster defeated will not cause this effect)."},{"title":"◯Delicate Loot","description":"If Lightning-type damage is dealt to this monster at least once, the loot &quot;Advanced Signal Circuit&quot; will be changed to &quot;Broken Magitech Components (50G/Black B).&quot;"},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Magitech HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Magitech's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Magitech can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Advanced Signal Circuit (800G/Black White A)"},{"roll":"2 - 8","loot":"Magitech Components (300G/Black White A)"},{"roll":"9 - 11","loot":"Rare Magitech Components (900G/Black White A)"},{"roll":"12+","loot":"Mysterious Magitech Components (2,400G/Black White A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Vox Queen","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"yJbsZMPHWEdal5s8","name":"Galil","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:galil","level":4,"monsterType":"Magitech","intelligence":"Servant","perception":"Mechanical","disposition":"Instructed","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Grasslands, Wastelands","reputation":10,"weakness":13,"weakPoint":"Lightning damage +3 points","initiative":11,"movementSpeed":"22 (Wheeled)","fortitude":"5 (12)","willpower":"5 (12)","source":"Natural History of Dorden p. 129","description":"This is a large self-powered wheel created during the Magitech Civilization Period. It measures 1.5m to 2m in length, with its entire body forming a circular wheel.\n\nIts original purpose was to be attached to large cargo or magic-powered trains, designed to traverse rough terrain beyond rails. However, these wheels are now either running wild after being abandoned or are being maliciously controlled by someone.\n\nWhen moving, it rotates itself like a monowheel and attacks by ramming into targets.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Slam","accuracy":"6 (13)","damage":"2d+5","evasion":"5 (12)","defense":4,"hp":{"value":30,"max":30},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Mechanical Body","description":"It is immune to criticals from edged weapons."},{"title":"►Rotational Friction / 4 (11) / Willpower / Negates","description":"Rapidly spinning itself, it creates intense friction against the floor or ground, producing a loud scraping sound. Within &quot;Range: Caster&quot; and &quot;Target: 1 Area (6m radius)/All,&quot; targets receive a -1 penalty to action checks for 10 seconds (1 round).\nThis ability can be used simultaneously by multiple Galils if they exist within the effect range. In such cases, for each additional character using the ability, this ability gains a +1 bonus to its Success Value (2 Galils for +1, 3 for +2, maximum of 4 for +3)."},{"title":"◯Delicate Loot","description":"If HP drops to 0 or less with magic damage, the loot from the &quot;Rotation Mechanism&quot; will be lost."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Magitech HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Magitech's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Magitech can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Iron (20G/Black B)"},{"roll":"Always","loot":"Rotation Mechanism (150G/Black White A)"},{"roll":"2 - 9","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"10+","loot":"Crude Magitech Components (100G/Black White A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Galil","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"zrUvbRurMtL9smHV","name":"Dorn","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:dorn","level":2,"monsterType":"Magitech","intelligence":"Servant","perception":"Mechanical","disposition":"Instructed","soulscars":0,"languages":"None","habitat":"Ruins, Settlements","reputation":9,"weakness":12,"weakPoint":"Lightning damage +3 points","initiative":8,"movementSpeed":"13 (Wheels)","fortitude":"3 (10)","willpower":"3 (10)","source":"CR I p. 423","description":"This security Magitech was produced in large numbers during the Magitech Civilization Period.\n\nIt is about one meter long and appears like a large Human child, and its entire body is covered with hard metal. It has one arm, a large hammer, which it wields to attack. With wheels mounted on its legs, it is more agile than it appears.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Hammer","accuracy":"3 (10)","damage":"2d+4","evasion":"3 (10)","defense":2,"hp":{"value":18,"max":18},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Mechanical Body","description":"It is immune to criticals from edged weapons."},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Magitech HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Magitech's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Magitech can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Iron (20G/Black B)"},{"roll":"2 - 10","loot":"Nothing"},{"roll":"11+","loot":"Crude Magitech Components (100G/Black White A)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Dorn","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"zuD0LzmL8AbyL4Je","name":"Maris Barba","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:maris-barba","level":8,"monsterType":"Magitech","intelligence":"Servant","perception":"Mechanical","disposition":"Instructed","soulscars":0,"languages":"Magitech","habitat":"Ruins, Mountains","reputation":15,"weakness":18,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":15,"movementSpeed":"-/10(Floating)","fortitude":"10 (17)","willpower":"11 (18)","source":"CR III p. 387","description":"This is a mid-air support type of the larger Barba series . At the end of the Magitech Civilization Period, Maris Barba's troops in formation were recorded to have attacked and defeated all the Barbarous.\n\nHowever, there is a record of problems such as inferior fighting capability and increased cost as a result of the larger size.","combatStyles":[{"style":"Machine Gun (Body)","accuracy":"11 (18)","damage":"2d+8","evasion":"11 (18)","defense":6,"hp":{"value":61,"max":61},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}},{"style":"Legs (Legs)","accuracy":"11 (18)","damage":"2d+10","evasion":"10 (17)","defense":7,"hp":{"value":66,"max":66},"mp":{"value":0,"max":0}}],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"All Sections","description":""},{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity, ◯ Psychic Type Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Limited Healing","description":"Effects which can heal Magitech HP are very limited, and mostly come from Spiritualism Magic and some special items.\nHealing effects such as Divine Magic, Fairy Magic, and Nature Magic cannot restore a Magitech's HP."},{"title":"◯ Can Be Detected","description":"Magitech can be detected with the [ Sense Magic ] spell and similar effects."},{"title":"Body","description":""},{"title":"◯ Gun","description":"The Machine Gun is treated as a gun weapon with a &quot;Range: 2 (20m)&quot; and a maximum magazine of 3.\nWhen the bullets run out, Maris Barba cannot attack at all."},{"title":"► Reload (One Time Only)","description":"Completely reloads the bullets of the Machine Gun. This effect can only be used once."},{"title":"◯ Targeting &amp; Hawk Eye","description":"Stray shots cannot occur. It also can aim through skirmishes at targets on the other side."},{"title":"Legs","description":""},{"title":"► Bursting Shell Drop/10 (17)/Willpower/ Half","description":"The bursting shell is dropped on the top of the target. With &quot;Range: Caster,&quot; this attack deals 2d+10 Fire magic damage to &quot;Target: 1 area (3m Radius) / 5&quot;.\nThis ability can only be used once."},{"title":"► Sprinkle Repair Liquid/Can't","description":"Sprays Magitech restoring liquid to &quot;Target: 1 area (3m Radius)/5&quot; in &quot;Range: Caster.&quot; If the target is a Magitech character, its HP is restored by 2d+7 points.\nThis effect can be used only once. This monster is always excluded from this effect."}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"Always","loot":"Iron (20G/Black B)"},{"roll":"2 - 7","loot":"Magitech Components (300G/Black White A)"},{"roll":"8 - 10","loot":"Rare Magitech Components (900G/Black White A)"},{"roll":"11+","loot":"Mysterious Magitech Components (2,400G/Black White S)"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Maris Barba","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}